    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/brown-cs.md",
    "title": "Brown — MS",
    "body": "# Brown — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#27 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Brown University\n\nDegree route: ScM in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nBrown CS ScM: 8 graded graduate courses within ~2 years (or ~1.5–16 months accelerated). Comprehensive or AI/ML tracks; optional professional internships and CSCI 2980 research project.\n\nOrientation: 8 courses · Comprehensive or AI/ML · ~1.5–2 years\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$43,908 — Academic-year tuition (ScM Computer Science, 4 courses × per-course rate); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nBrown Student Financial Services / Graduate Funding COA 2026–27: Computer Science master’s per-course rate $10,977. Standard track for ScM CS is 8 courses; COA budgets 2 courses/term → AY tuition $21,954 × 2 = $43,908. Estimated total program tuition at the published rate = $87,816. Mandatory fees in the COA (~$1,596 AY at the 2+2 pattern) and health insurance are separate. Program may also be completed as 8 courses in one year.\n\nApplication timing: Fall: 15 Jan (month-day; year not labeled) · Spring: 1 Nov · Fifth-year Fall: 1 May. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GRE General not required but score submission is encouraged. GRE Subject not required. If supplied, strong results expected (CS applications page).\n- GMAT: not_required — Pure CS ScM; GMAT not part of program requirements.\n- TOEFL: required — min 105 — Required for intl applicants whose native language is not English unless exempt. TOEFL iBT on/before Jan 20 2026: min 105. On/after Jan 21 2026: min 5.0 (5.5+ strongly recommended). No MyBest/Superscores. Code 3094.\n- IELTS: required — min 8 — IELTS minimum overall 8.0 per CS ScM program page (above general master’s recommended 7).\n- English waiver: Not required if degree from institution where English is sole language of instruction, or from listed countries (Australia, Bahamas, Botswana, Cameroon, Canada except Quebec, Ethiopia, Ghana, Ireland, Kenya, Lesotho, Liberia, Malawi, New Zealand, Nigeria, Zimbabwe, South Africa, Sierra Leone, Swaziland, Tanzania, Gambia, Uganda, UK, West Indies, Zambia).\n- GPA: not_stated — No numeric minimum GPA on CS ScM graduateprograms page; seeks outstanding students with CS/equivalent background.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 3 — 3 letters for external applications; 2 for Brown fifth-year. Recent grads (≤3 years) / current students: at least 2 from professors who can speak to CS coursework.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Personal Statement / program questions — Master’s application process requires Personal Statement and/or short-answer/program questions (see application).\n- Resume: required — Resume/CV required (CS ScM application requirements).\n- Transcripts: required — Unofficial OK for application; official only for enrolling students. Non-U.S. degrees: WES/ECE/The Evaluation Company evaluation required before enrollment. Undergrads: include Fall grades when available.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not described on CS ScM program or CS applications pages.\n- Fee: waivers: Need-based waiver via form in application; veterans/active-duty military eligible with documentation (Master’s Programs FAQ). — Dollar amount not stated on CS ScM or CS applications pages as of scrape; confirm in online application.\n- Other: On-campus ScM (Comprehensive) and AI/ML track (campus or online) — same degree family\n- Other: Fall deadline Jan 15 (intl & final); Spring Nov 1 (intl Oct 1); fifth-year May 1 Fall / Nov 1 Spring\n- Other: Prereq-style background: intro programming, algorithms/DS, systems or SE, discrete math/probability, linear algebra + one advanced CS course\n\nGRE optional but encouraged. IELTS bar is high (8.0). Distinguish on-campus Comprehensive vs AI/ML track. Fee amount confirm in portal.\n\n- [CS ScM application requirements](https://graduateprograms.brown.edu/graduate-program/computer-science-scm)\n- [Brown CS Applying](https://cs.brown.edu/degrees/masters/applications/)\n- [Master’s application process](https://masters.brown.edu/admissions/application-process)\n- [Master’s Programs FAQ (fee waivers)](https://masters.brown.edu/admissions/masters-programs-faq)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MS overview](https://cs.brown.edu/degrees/masters/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://sfs.brown.edu/tuition-and-fees/graduate)\n- [COA by program (CS)](https://gradfunding.brown.edu/cost-attendance-program)\n- [Graduate Programs ScM Computer Science (deadlines)](https://graduateprograms.brown.edu/graduate-program/computer-science-scm)\n- [Brown CS Applying to Master's](https://cs.brown.edu/degrees/masters/applications/)\n- [SPS Deadlines and Credits (CS Fall Jan. 15)](https://masters.brown.edu/admissions/tuition-aid/deadlines-credits)\n- [Comprehensive track requirements](https://cs.brown.edu/degrees/masters/reqs/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
