    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/caltech-cs.md",
    "title": "Caltech — PhD route",
    "body": "# Caltech — PhD route\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#12 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: California Institute of Technology\n\nDegree route: Computer Science graduate department\n\nApplication status: No standard terminal master’s\n\n## Academic direction\n\nCaltech CMS: no direct terminal MS admissions. Applicants enter the PhD; MS may be awarded only in exceptional en-route cases.\n\nOrientation: Restricted · PhD-only admissions\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$68,574 — Academic-year tuition (Institute graduate) — restricted / PhD-path MS only; 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total. Availability: CMS admits only PhD-track students; MS awarded by petition, not as an open terminal master’s.\n\nCaltech Graduate Studies Estimated Budget 2026–27: Tuition $68,574 annual ($22,858/term × 3); Mandatory Fees $2,448 (total tuition+mandatory fees $71,022). Computing and Mathematical Sciences (CMS) catalog: only students who expect to pursue the Ph.D. are admitted; PhD students in good standing may petition to add the MS after course requirements. No open external terminal MS CS for Fall 2027. Published Institute tuition recorded with that availability note. Stipend packages typically cover tuition for funded PhD students.\n\nApplication timing: No external Fall 2027 MS deadline — CMS admits PhD-track only; MS by petition after courses (not open terminal MS). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: not_required — CMS Graduate Programs FAQ: GRE not required for application for the 2026–2027 academic year.\n- GMAT: not_accepted — PhD STEM route; GMAT not used.\n- TOEFL: optional — Grad Studies FAQ: English proficiency exams not required for admission; applicants whose native language is not English or who lack English-medium degree should demonstrate strong English. TOEFL recognized; self-report OK. Institution code 4034. No published minimum.\n- IELTS: optional — IELTS, PTE, Duolingo and other certified exams recognized; not required for admission; no published minimum.\n- English waiver: Exemptions noted for applicants who studied in the U.S. ≥2 years or received a degree where English is primary language of instruction (Grad Studies FAQ). ESL placement may occur after arrival.\n- GPA: not_stated — scale 4 — No minimum GPA. Most successful applicants have U.S. GPA ≥3.5/4.0 and/or top 5–10% of class (Grad Studies FAQ).\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 3 — Three letters required; online application accepts three maximum (Grad Studies FAQ / checklist).\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Essays / statement — Essays required components of application (Grad Studies checklist: transcripts, 3 LORs, CV, essays).\n- Resume: required — CV required (Grad Studies application checklist).\n- Transcripts: required — Transcripts from each college/university attended required; upload most recent available with application.\n- Interview: by_invitation — Most options host visit days for select applicants; online interviews may be conducted when in-person visits not feasible (Grad Studies FAQ).\n- Fee: $100 — waivers: Limited waivers for financial need or affiliated organizations; request in online application payment options with hardship documentation. — $100 USD application fee (Graduate Studies Apply Online).\n- Other: NO EXTERNAL TERMINAL MS: CMS catalog — only students who expect to pursue the Ph.D. are admitted; master’s awarded only in exceptional cases\n- Other: CMS FAQ: traditionally do not offer Master’s as a terminal degree\n- Other: Apply to PhD (CS / CMS / ACM / CDS options); deadline Dec 15 (CMS pages also mention Dec 1 review start)\n- Other: Full-time only; funding typically with PhD admission\n\nDo not treat as an external MS target—PhD-route only. Terminal MS not offered. GRE not required 2026–27.\n\n- [CMS Graduate Programs FAQ](https://www.cms.caltech.edu/academics/grad)\n- [Catalog CMS special regulations (MS exceptional)](https://www.catalog.caltech.edu/current/information-for-graduate-students/special-regulations-for-graduate-options/computing-and-mathematical-science-cms/)\n- [Grad Studies Apply Online (fee)](https://gradoffice.caltech.edu/admissions/applyonline)\n- [Grad Studies FAQ for applicants](https://gradoffice.caltech.edu/admissions/faq-applicants)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CMS graduate programs](https://www.cms.caltech.edu/academics/grad)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.gradoffice.caltech.edu/financialsupport/budget)\n- [CMS catalog special regulations (MS by petition)](https://catalog.caltech.edu/current/information-for-graduate-students/special-regulations-for-graduate-options/computing-and-mathematical-science-cms/)\n- [CMS catalog regulations](https://www.catalog.caltech.edu/current/information-for-graduate-students/special-regulations-for-graduate-options/computing-and-mathematical-science-cms/)\n- [Graduate admissions FAQ](https://gradoffice.caltech.edu/admissions/faq-applicants)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
