    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/columbia-cs.md",
    "title": "Columbia — MS",
    "body": "# Columbia — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#15 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Columbia University\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nColumbia CS MS: ≥30 points, designed for ~3 semesters, with breadth, PDL, and ≥6 points at 6000-level. Eight faculty pathways plus Personalized/Thesis by invite.\n\nOrientation: 30 points · Pathways · ~3 semesters\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$67,728 — Academic-year tuition (SEAS MS, $2,822/point × 12 points × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nColumbia Engineering Graduate Tuition bulletin and SFS Graduate Engineering COA 2026–27: M.S. tuition $2,822 per credit/point. Full-time COA budgets 12 points/semester → $33,864/semester → $67,728 AY Fall+Spring. A typical 30-credit MS CS totals $84,660 in tuition across the degree (pace varies). Mandatory fees in the COA (health insurance, health service, university services, SEAS activities, document fee) and living costs are separate; CS is not listed with the IEOR/AI program fee.\n\nApplication timing: Fall priority 15 Jan · Fall final/regular 15 Feb 2027 (CVN year-labeled for Fall 2027) · Spring 15 Oct. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — Fall 2027 Engineering brochure: GRE scores optional for 2027. CS FAQ points to SEAS application-requirements for official GRE policy. Code 2111.\n- GMAT: not_required — CS MS uses GRE optional policy; GMAT not listed among CS/SEAS MS materials.\n- TOEFL: required — min 101 — TOEFL, IELTS, or PTE Academic required per CS FAQ unless SEAS exception. Recommended TOEFL iBT total 101 (recommended, not hard floor in FAQ). DET also listed on 2027 brochure. Code 2111. Scores must remain valid through start of classes.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — Recommended IELTS 7 for admission (CS FAQ). Enter TRF / e-download to Columbia.\n- English waiver: See SEAS policy for exceptions (e.g., degree from exempt countries); contact seasgradmit@columbia.edu. Brochure lists TOEFL/IELTS/DET/PTE if applicable.\n- GPA: not_stated — No minimum GPA to apply; successful applicants typically GPA ≥3.5 (CS FAQ).\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 3 — Three letters of recommendation (SEAS Fall 2027 brochure Application Requirements). Electronic submission required.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Personal Statement — Personal Statement (CS FAQ: typically 250–1000 words preferred; topics include reasons for program, experience, career goals). Listed on SEAS brochure.\n- Resume: required — Resume or CV required (SEAS Fall 2027 brochure).\n- Transcripts: required — University transcripts required (SEAS brochure). Non-English transcript policy administered by SEAS GSA.\n- Interview: required — Video Interview required for MS programs (SEAS Fall 2027 brochure).\n- Fee: $85 — waivers: Confirm current SEAS waiver policy on application portal / admissions FAQs. — $85 application fee (SEAS Fall 2027 brochure).\n- Other: Fall priority Jan 15 / final Feb 15; Spring Oct 15\n- Other: Non-CS undergrad: typically ≥4 CS foundation/programming courses + 2 math, or Bridge pathway\n- Other: No Summer admit; Columbia does not defer admission\n\nComplete video interview. GRE optional for 2027. Prefer Jan 15 priority deadline.\n\n- [CS MS Application FAQ](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/ms/appfaq/)\n- [SEAS Fall 2027 brochure (PDF)](https://www.engineering.columbia.edu/sites/default/files/2026-09/Tri-fold_9-22-26.pdf)\n- [SEAS application requirements (official pointer)](https://www.gradengineering.columbia.edu/graduate-admissions/application-requirements)\n- [CS MS program](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/ms/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMS pathways page; department funding for MS not verified as guaranteed. Do not apply PhD funding.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MS overview](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/ms/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://sfs.columbia.edu/content/graduate-engineering-cost-attendance)\n- [SEAS graduate tuition bulletin](https://bulletin.columbia.edu/columbia-engineering/graduate-studies/graduate-tuition-fees-payments/)\n- [CS Admissions (MS deadlines table)](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/admissions8/)\n- [MS Program Application FAQ](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/ms/appfaq/)\n- [CVN Computer Science Master's (Fall 2027 / Spring 2027 year-labeled)](https://cvn.columbia.edu/content/computer-science-masters-degree)\n- [MS requirements FAQ](https://www.cs.columbia.edu/education/ms/regfaq/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
