    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/mit-cs.md",
    "title": "MIT — PhD route",
    "body": "# MIT — PhD route\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#1 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Massachusetts Institute of Technology\n\nDegree route: EECS graduate department\n\nApplication status: No external terminal master’s\n\n## Academic direction\n\nMIT EECS does not offer a terminal master’s for external applicants. MEng is for MIT EECS undergrads; SM is typically PhD-en-route (or special programs like LGO).\n\nOrientation: Restricted · No external terminal MS\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$66,720 — Academic-year tuition (full regular graduate × 2 terms) — restricted route; 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total. Availability: EECS MEng is open only to MIT undergraduates (not an external terminal MS).\n\nMIT Registrar Graduate tuition 2026–27: Full regular tuition $33,360 per fall/spring term → $66,720 AY. EECS MEng is a fifth-year bachelor’s/master’s path for MIT undergraduates in listed Course 6 programs only; MIT does not offer a general external-admission terminal MS in CS/EECS for Fall 2027 applicants. Published rate recorded for sticker reference with that availability restriction. Miscellaneous fees and living costs separate.\n\nApplication timing: No external Fall 2027 MS deadline — EECS MEng is MIT-undergrad-only; external graduate admission is PhD-track only. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: not_required — EECS Graduate Admissions Information Letter and OGE program page: department does NOT require GRE scores for admission.\n- GMAT: not_required — Not used for EECS PhD admissions.\n- TOEFL: required — min 100 — International students: TOEFL iBT minimum 100; institute code 3514; department code 78 or 66. OGE: IELTS preferred over TOEFL; waiver may be available.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS minimum 7; electronic scores to MIT Graduate Admissions. EECS letter: IELTS can be used if TOEFL unavailable; same waiver cases as TOEFL.\n- English waiver: EECS letter: TOEFL/IELTS may be waived e.g. if applicant has been in the U.S. at least two years, or if country's first language is English. OGE notes waiver of TOEFL/IELTS may be available.\n- GPA: not_stated — EECS letter: admission influenced by GPA but there is not an official cut-off.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 3 — Three letters of recommendation required (EECS letter and OGE application requirements).\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as statement of objectives; essays — OGE: Essay 1 research activities and goals; Essay 2 academic and intellectual journey. EECS letter refers to Statement of Objectives detailing research interests.\n- Resume: not_stated — Resume/CV not explicitly listed on OGE EECS application-requirements block reviewed (online application, two essays, three LORs, transcripts, English scores).\n- Transcripts: required — Transcripts required; admitted students submit official transcript(s) to EECS Graduate Office. Do not send published papers or theses with application.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not stated on OGE EECS program page or EECS admissions information letter reviewed.\n- Fee: $90 — waivers: Applicants can request a fee waiver via OGE eligibility criteria / EECS fee-waiver link. — OGE EECS listing: application fee $90.00.\n- Other: FLAG — NO EXTERNAL TERMINAL MASTER'S: Department does not offer admission for a terminal master's. Apply for PhD; SM earned en route if needed. MEng degrees restricted to MIT undergraduates only.\n- Other: Application opens Sep 15; deadline Dec 1 11:59 p.m. Eastern; Fall Term (September); Summer only for LGO.\n- Other: Extremely competitive; strong background in math, physics, engineering, or CS expected.\n- Other: PhD students typically supported by fellowship/RA/TA (tuition, stipend, medical insurance).\n\nFlag as PhD-only / no external MS for Fall 2027 slate. Requirements above are for the EECS PhD application path only.\n\n- [MIT OGE EECS program page](https://oge.mit.edu/programs/electrical-engineering-and-computer-science/)\n- [MIT EECS Graduate Admissions Information Letter](https://www.eecs.mit.edu/graduate-admissions-information-letter/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-061, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program / academic source](https://www.eecs.mit.edu/graduate-admissions-information-letter/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://registrar.mit.edu/registration-academics/tuition-fees/graduate)\n- [MEng program](https://www.eecs.mit.edu/academics/undergraduate-programs/meng-program/)\n- [EECS Admission Process](https://www.eecs.mit.edu/academics/graduate-programs/admission-process/)\n- [EECS graduate admissions FAQs](https://www.eecs.mit.edu/academics/graduate-programs/admission-process/graduate-admissions-faqs/)\n- [OGE EECS programs](https://oge.mit.edu/programs/electrical-engineering-and-computer-science/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
