    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/penn-cs.md",
    "title": "Penn — MS",
    "body": "# Penn — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#19 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Pennsylvania\n\nDegree route: MSE in Computer and Information Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nPenn CIS MSE: 10 course units with four constrained cores (theory + systems rules), CIS electives, and optional thesis (CIS 9990). Complete within seven years; min GPA 2.7.\n\nOrientation: 10 CUs · Constrained cores · Optional thesis\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$52,950 — Academic-year tuition (SEAS on-campus master’s, 3 CUs × 2 semesters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nPenn SRFS SEAS on-campus master’s 2026–27: tuition $8,825 per course unit (CU). Catalog CIS MSE requires 10 CUs; sample plans use 3 CUs in a typical Fall or Spring term → AY tuition reference $8,825 × 3 × 2 = $52,950. At 4 CUs/term: $35,300/semester ($70,600 AY). Mandatory fees at 3 CUs: General Fee $2,134 + Technology Fee $405 + Clinical Fee $385 (semester totals with tuition $29,399)—fees not included in the tuition figure. Full 10-CU degree tuition at $8,825 = $88,250. Online Engineering rates differ.\n\nApplication timing: Apps open 15 Sep 2026 · Early 1 Nov 2026 · 11:59 p.m. EST · Regular 1 Feb 2027 · 11:59 p.m. EST (CIS MSE Fall 2027). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — Penn Engineering: GRE optional for current master's cycle (Fall 2027 open Sep 15, 2026–Feb 1, 2027). Omitting does not hurt; valid scores encouraged if available. Institution code 2888; scores valid 5 years; official scores by deadline.\n- GMAT: not_required — Pure CIS MSE; GMAT not listed on Penn Engineering How to Apply.\n- TOEFL: required — International / non-US citizen/PR whose native language is not English must submit TOEFL iBT (code 2888), IELTS, or DET. No hard minimum for admission; recommended TOEFL 5.0 (or 100 legacy 0–120). At-home TOEFL accepted. Scores valid 2 years; exam by deadline.\n- IELTS: required — IELTS accepted; recommended 7.5. Send electronically to “University of Pennsylvania School of Engineering and Applied Science.” At-home IELTS accepted.\n- English waiver: Waived if by matriculation applicant: graduates from a U.S. program; attends school in a country where English is official language; or graduates from an institution where English is the medium of instruction (indicated on unofficial transcript). Waiver processed after submit (3–5 business days).\n- GPA: not_stated — No admission minimum GPA stated on Penn Engineering How to Apply. CIS MSE expects strong undergrad math/CS preparation (OS, PL, DS, discrete math, linear algebra, algorithms/theory).\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two letters for master's (three only for CIS Ph.D. / BE Ph.D. Medical Physics). Include one from a faculty member familiar with scholarly abilities. Submitted via application email link.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Personal Statement — Personal statement ≤2 pages answering: interest in program; candidacy; benefit; contribution to Penn Engineering community; reasons for success; post-completion plans.\n- Resume: required — Professional resume covering job skills, depth of professional experience, leadership.\n- Transcripts: required — Unofficial transcript from each university/college with course credit; English with grade key; name, institution, courses, credit hours, grades. Official transcripts only if admitted and enroll.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not mentioned on Penn Engineering How to Apply.\n- Fee: $95 — waivers: Auto-waived if US citizen/PR with proven low-income; Penn or U.S. military affiliation; or eligible US partner-institution Accelerated Master’s applicant. — $95 nonrefundable with online application.\n- Other: Distinct from MCIT (conversion); non-CS undergrads directed toward MCIT/MAS-CS routes.\n- Other: Fall 2027 master's: early CIS deadline Nov 1, 2026 11:59pm EST; regular Feb 1, 2027; decisions by Apr 1.\n- Other: DET accepted (recommended 135).\n\nApply via Penn Engineering Grad Admissions (not catalog curriculum page). Early Nov 1 for CIS if seeking early review. GRE optional≠waived. Confirm Fall 2027 fee/waiver categories on live how-to-apply.\n\n- [Penn Engineering How to Apply (Fall 2027)](https://gradadm.seas.upenn.edu/how-to-apply/)\n- [Penn Engineering Master's Programs timeline](https://gradadm.seas.upenn.edu/masters/)\n- [CIS MSE program overview](https://www.cis.upenn.edu/mse-in-cis/)\n- [Catalog CIS MSE (curriculum)](https://catalog.upenn.edu/graduate/programs/computer-information-science-mse/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CIS MSE catalog](https://catalog.upenn.edu/graduate/programs/computer-information-science-mse/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://srfs.upenn.edu/costs-budgeting/seas)\n- [Residential master’s CS admissions](https://gradadm.engineering.upenn.edu/residential-masters/computer-science/)\n- [Penn Engineering How to Apply (Fall 2027 master's timeline)](https://gradadm.engineering.upenn.edu/how-to-apply/)\n- [Penn Engineering Master's Programs (CIS early deadline noted)](https://gradadm.engineering.upenn.edu/masters/)\n- [MSE in CIS requirements](https://www.cis.upenn.edu/mse-in-cis-requirements/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
