    "path": "02-computer-science/programs/ucla-cs.md",
    "title": "UCLA — MS",
    "body": "# UCLA — MS\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#15 (tie) in U.S. News Best Computer Science Schools · graduate departments, April 2026 release.\n\n33 departments occupy ranks 1–27. All seven schools tied at 27 are included. This is a graduate department ranking, not a ranking of the specific master’s routes listed here.\n\nRanking provenance: [IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of California, Los Angeles\n\nDegree route: MS in Computer Science\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUCLA CS MS: nine 4-unit courses (B- or better) plus three CS 201 seminars. Thesis (CS 598) or Capstone project plans; no fixed core list — majority CS coursework.\n\nOrientation: 36 units · Thesis or capstone · Flexible coursework\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$38,233 — Academic-year tuition and mandatory fees (Academic Master, nonresident, continuing); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUCLA Registrar public fee tables Academic Master annual 2026–27 nonresident continuing total $38,232.76 (Tuition $13,722 + NRST $15,102 + Student Services Fee $1,344 + UCSHIP $7,516.98 + campus fees). California resident continuing total without NRST $23,130.76. Grad Division rounds these to about $38,233 / $23,131. New students add one-time Document Fee $97.43. CS MS uses the standard Academic Master schedule (not a self-supporting program). NRST PhD candidacy waiver does not apply to MS.\n\nApplication timing: Apps mid-Sep · Deadline 15 Dec 2026 · 23:59 Pacific (MS/PhD Fall only — Grad Division 2027–28). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: not_required — UCLA Grad Division 2026–2027 Computer Science admission requirements table: GRE: Not required. CS department page still carries Fall 2025–2026 optional-language for that prior cycle; for 2026–2027 cycle prefer Grad Division “Not required.” GMAT may not be substituted. Subject GRE not reviewed.\n- GMAT: not_accepted — CS Graduate Application Requirements: GMAT may not be substituted for the GRE.\n- TOEFL: required — min 87 — Intl / non-exempt: TOEFL iBT ≥87 (legacy) or overall ≥4.5 new scale (tests on/after Jan 21, 2026) per Grad English Requirements / CS page. UCLA code 4837; CS dept code 78. Valid within 2 years of application submit. Duolingo not accepted. FAQ also cites legacy subscores W25/S24/R21/L17.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS Academic overall ≥7.0. Send to major department and Division of Graduate Education.\n- English waiver: Exempt if bachelor’s or higher from accredited U.S. university or from country where English is sole language of instruction per WHED; or completed two years full-time study at such institutions. Citizenship alone does not exempt.\n- GPA: required — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — University cumulative GPA ≥3.0 for consideration. Dept reviews ≥3.0; most competitive ≥3.5 undergrad and ≥3.50 any graduate study; average admitted ~3.60.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 3 — At least three letters via online application by Dec 15. MS: prefer professors from junior/senior years. (ESAP MS has special 2-letter CS-faculty rule.)\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Statement of Purpose (+ Personal Statement) — SOP 500-word limit in online application (prompts on Grad Division site). Also required Personal Statement 500-word limit. SOP serves as writing sample.\n- Resume: optional — Resume/vitae not required; awards/distinctions/publications may be entered in online application sections instead.\n- Transcripts: required — Upload one official transcript per post-secondary institution in online application by Dec 15. Final official docs after offer. China/India specific degree-certificate rules on CS page. UCLA students: MyUCLA record OK.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not listed among CS graduate application requirements.\n- Fee: $155 — waivers: Need-based and special-program waivers for eligible U.S. citizens/PR (and listed programs) per Grad Admissions FAQs; upload docs in Fee Waiver section. No exceptions beyond stated criteria. — UCLA Grad Admissions FAQ: $135 U.S. citizens/PR; $155 all other applicants. amountUsd = international rate.\n- Other: Fall only; deadline Dec 15 23:59 Pacific. Apply mid-Sep–Dec 15.\n- Other: Apply to MS or PhD—not both. Applicants who already hold an MS in CS or closely related field not considered for MS.\n- Other: MS funding: not eligible for departmental support; TA/GSR/reader not guaranteed; intl MS must show ≥~$65,000 first-year support for visa if admitted.\n- Other: Program-requirements Grad page is degree requirements (thesis/capstone), not admissions checklist—use CS graduate-requirements.\n\nUse cs.ucla.edu/graduate-requirements/ + Grad Division 2026–2027 deptinfo for GRE. Do not rely on curriculum-only Grad program-requirements URL alone.\n\n- [UCLA CS Graduate Application Requirements](https://www.cs.ucla.edu/graduate-requirements/)\n- [UCLA Grad Division 2026–2027 CS Admission Requirements](https://grad.ucla.edu/gasaa/deptinfo/deptinfo.asp?academicyear=20262027&code=0201)\n- [UCLA English Requirements](https://grad.ucla.edu/admissions/english-requirements/)\n- [UCLA Admissions FAQs (fee)](https://grad.ucla.edu/admissions/faqs/)\n- [UCLA Grad Program Requirements CS (degree plans)](https://grad.ucla.edu/graduate-program-requirements/program-requirements-for-computer-science-7-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nThe department explicitly does not guarantee TA, graduate student researcher or reader positions to MS students.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-016, SCH-017, SCH-018, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-021, SCH-038, SCH-039, SCH-040, SCH-041, SCH-042, SCH-043, SCH-044, SCH-045, SCH-059, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-073, SCH-074, SCH-079, SCH-080, SCH-081, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CS Graduate Admissions](https://www.cs.ucla.edu/graduate-admissions/)\n- [Official tuition / budget (Registrar public fees)](https://sa.ucla.edu/RO/Fees/Public/public-fees)\n- [Grad Division tuition summary](https://grad.ucla.edu/funding/tuition/)\n- [Financial aid COA](https://financialaid.ucla.edu/graduate-aid/cost-of-attendance)\n- [CS Graduate Application Requirements (Dec 15 23:59 PT; mid-Sep open)](https://www.cs.ucla.edu/graduate-requirements/)\n- [UCLA Grad Division CS 2027–2028 requirements (deadline Dec 15, 2026)](https://grad.ucla.edu/gasaa/deptinfo/deptinfo.asp?academicyear=20272028&code=0201)\n- [CS Grad Admissions FAQ](https://www.cs.ucla.edu/graduate-admission-frequently-asked-questions/)\n- [Program requirements (Grad Division)](https://grad.ucla.edu/graduate-program-requirements/program-requirements-for-computer-science-7-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2/)\n- [Graduate student handbook](https://www.cs.ucla.edu/graduate-student-handbook/)\n- [U.S. News positions via IvyPath Advisory](https://www.ivypath-advisory.com/ranking/major-cs-us/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
