    "path": "03-business/programs/cmu-mba.md",
    "title": "CMU Tepper — MBA",
    "body": "# CMU Tepper — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#16 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Carnegie Mellon University\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nTepper Full-Time MBA: ~21 months, 192 units, mini-semester format with early electives and final-mini capstone. Accelerated option separate.\n\nOrientation: ~21 months · 192 units · Mini-semesters\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$84,186 — Academic-year tuition (Tepper Full-Time MBA); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nCMU Student Financial Services Tepper Full-Time MBA and Accelerated MBA page for 2026–2027 lists Tuition $42,093 Fall 2026 + $42,093 Spring 2027 = $84,186 academic year. University fees (activity $248, transportation $302, technology $490 AY), health insurance ($3,352), and living expenses are separate; single-student total budget $120,798. Full-Time MBA is four semesters; Accelerated is three — figure is one academic year only. Laptop estimate $1,500 additional. Full-time MBA only — not part-time/online.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 8 Jan 2027 (Full-Time MBA; R1 passed; clock time not on table). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — GMAT, GMAT Focus, GRE, or EA required unless approved test waiver. GRE code Carnegie Mellon Tepper 4883. Scores valid 5 years at submit. Waiver case-by-case for academic readiness; does not signal admission; scholarship eligibility unaffected. Pre-check eligibility form available.\n- GMAT: required — GMAT/GMAT Focus Full-Time MBA code 69H-XH-99; EA accepted (strong quant coursework and/or STEM professional experience expected). No superscore as official; holistic review of all submitted scores. Waiver alternative available case-by-case.\n- TOEFL: required — TOEFL required unless bachelor’s or graduate degree with sole language of instruction English. Recommended iBT 25 each section; new TOEFL iBT overall ≥5 with section ≥5. Code 2074 Carnegie Mellon Graduate Business. Valid 2 years.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — Recommended IELTS overall 7 and 7 in each band. Select Carnegie Mellon and Tepper. Duolingo DET also accepted (recommended overall 120).\n- English waiver: Waived if bachelor’s (or graduate—recommend still testing) from institution where sole language of instruction was English. Non-U.S. degrees: documents must state English sole medium for entire university, or upload official Registrar letter.\n- GPA: not_stated — No published minimum GPA. Prerequisite: one semester college-level calculus with letter grade B or better (or complete Tepper Calculus Fundamentals before matriculation).\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 1 — One professional recommendation; ideally current/previous supervisor. GMAC Common LOR.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Written essay + video goals essay — One required written essay (max 500 words)—choose 1 of 2 prompts (uncertainty/action or professional/personal transformation). Required video essay on post-MBA career goals (up to 2 minutes). Optional essay for gaps/context/reapplicant strengthening.\n- Resume: required — 1–2 page resume; standard 12-pt font; include Month/Year start and end dates for each role.\n- Transcripts: required — Unofficial scanned university transcripts (not web/portal downloads) from all undergrad/grad; degree name/conferral; grading scale; translations if needed. Official after admit.\n- Interview: by_invitation — Evaluative behavioral interview by invitation only and required. Invitations may begin within one week of deadline through decision date.\n- Fee: $200 — waivers: May earn waiver by attending a Tepper event; reapplicants within last year waived. — $200 payable online by credit card at submission.\n- Other: Deadlines: R1 Sep 30 2026; R2 Jan 8 2027; R3 Mar 3 2027 (final for international FT); R4 May 5 2027; R4 Final Jun 15 2027\n- Other: Four-year bachelor’s or equivalent required\n- Other: Re Vera verification for admitted students who accept\n\nPlan GMAT/GRE/EA unless you obtain an approved waiver before/at review. Video essay is mandatory. International applicants: Round 3 is last FT round.\n\n- [Apply to Full-Time MBA](https://www.cmu.edu/tepper/programs/mba/admissions/apply-full-time-mba)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nTepper MBA scholarships not detailed on SFS tuition page; check Tepper admissions financial aid. Do not invent amounts.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-050, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-065, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MBA curriculum](https://www.cmu.edu/tepper/programs/mba/curriculum)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.cmu.edu/sfs/tuition/graduate/tepper/full-accel-mba.html)\n- [2026–2027 Graduate Tuition index](https://www.cmu.edu/sfs/tuition/graduate/index.html)\n- [Apply to Full-Time MBA (deadlines table)](https://www.cmu.edu/tepper/programs/mba/admissions/apply-full-time-mba)\n- [Full-Time MBA](https://www.cmu.edu/tepper/programs/mba/full-time)\n- [MBA programs hub](https://www.cmu.edu/tepper/programs/mba/)\n- [Curriculum map PDF](https://www.cmu.edu/sites/default/files/cmu-tepper-site-files/documents/full-time-mba-curriculum-map-24-25.pdf)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
