    "path": "03-business/programs/dartmouth-mba.md",
    "title": "Dartmouth Tuck — MBA",
    "body": "# Dartmouth Tuck — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#9 in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Dartmouth College\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nTuck MBA: 2 years, 76.5 credits (14-course core + electives). Integrated Y1 required curriculum; Y2 electives.\n\nOrientation: 2 years · 76.5 credits · 14-course core\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$87,536 — Academic-year tuition (Tuck MBA); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nTuck Cost of Attendance for Academic Year 2026–2027 lists Tuition $87,536 for Class of 2028 (on- or off-campus) and Class of 2027 (off-campus). Program fee is separate ($6,150 first-year / $5,440 second-year). Housing, food, and health insurance ($5,216) are separate. Footnote: tuition costs are for AY 2026–27 and subject to change; anticipate a 3–5% increase for 2027–28. First year is four terms; second year three terms on Tuck’s quarter schedule.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 5 Jan 2027 · 5:00 p.m. ET (Tuck; R1 passed). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — Must self-report GMAT or GRE (all versions accepted; no superscore; no minimum). Valid at submit; GRE code 4887. Case-by-case GMAT/GRE waiver if ≥2 years post-grad work, native English OR bachelor’s sole English instruction, request before deadlines (R1/Consortium1 Aug 12 2026; R2/C2 Nov 9 2026; R3 Mar 5 2027)—not automatic; miss deadline → must submit score that round.\n- GMAT: required — GMAT accepted (code Z04-NH-64). Same waiver request process/deadlines as GRE. Official scores for enrolling students; release early if score expires before Aug 1 2027.\n- TOEFL: required — Non-native English speakers must submit DET, IELTS Academic, PTE Academic, or TOEFL iBT unless bachelor’s from institution where English is sole language of instruction. No published minimum scores. TOEFL code D507. Online/at-home accepted. DET must be certified to Tuck before submit.\n- IELTS: required — IELTS Academic accepted; provide TRF number. No published minimum band on Apply page.\n- English waiver: Non-native speakers qualify if bachelor’s degree from institution where English is sole language of instruction—self-indicate in Degrees section; no separate approval documents required for that waiver.\n- GPA: not_stated — Report undergrad GPA and additional schools in Degrees section; committee calibrates across grading schemes—no published minimum.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two LORs (one new LOR if reapplicant from most recent cycle). Prefer current direct supervisor; explain if not. GMAC Common LOR questions. Professors/friends/family/coaches discouraged.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Application essays — Three required essays (2000 characters each): goals/growth/why Tuck; important aspect of who you are; supporting another person when difficult. Reapplicant essay additional. Optional information section (2000 chars).\n- Resume: required — Upload resume; encouraged one page covering undergrad-and-after experiences.\n- Transcripts: required — Upload transcript for every undergrad/grad school attended including grading scale; certified English translation if needed; transfer school transcripts required. Official via Re Vera after enrollment.\n- Interview: by_invitation — All admitted applicants interview before offer. Guaranteed interview if complete app (incl. tests + LORs) by Sep 1 2026 (R1/C1) or Dec 1 2026 (R2/C2) 5pm ET; otherwise invitational. Virtual and limited on-campus; 30–45 min with Tuck Admissions Associates.\n- Fee: $250 — waivers: Automatic one-time for listed groups (U.S. military active/veteran; recent Dartmouth/HACU/HBCU/TCU/Women’s College grads; UN LDCs; first-gen; Tuck undergrad programs; Discover Tuck visit attendees as of Jul 10 2026; etc.). Requestable with docs for Access Fellows, AmeriCorps, Forté, Fulbright, MLT, Pell, Peace Corps, TFA, etc.—≥2 business days before deadline. — Nonrefundable $250 USD; processing fees may apply.\n- Other: Rounds: R1 Sep 24 2026 5pm ET; R2 Jan 5 2027; R3 Mar 24 2027 (+ Consortium Oct 15 2026 / Jan 5 2027)\n- Other: Short-/long-term goals in Application Specifics (300 characters each)\n- Other: International applicants encouraged R1/R2 for visa timing\n\nGMAT/GRE required unless approved waiver before round-specific waiver deadline. Early complete apps can lock a guaranteed interview. No published English score floors—submit a solid DET/IELTS/TOEFL/PTE if not waived.\n\n- [Applying to Tuck](https://www.tuck.dartmouth.edu/admissions/apply)\n- [Interview with Tuck](https://www.tuck.dartmouth.edu/admissions/interview)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nTuck scholarships/fellowships pages under Finance Your Degree; intl eligibility typically yes for school merit aid — confirm each award.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-026, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Academic experience](https://tuck.dartmouth.edu/mba/academic-experience)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://tuck.dartmouth.edu/admissions/finance-your-degree/cost-attendance)\n- [Tuck Tuition and Costs](https://tuck.dartmouth.edu/admissions/finance-your-degree/tuition-and-costs)\n- [Scholarships and Fellowships](https://tuck.dartmouth.edu/admissions/finance-your-degree/scholarships-and-fellowships)\n- [Applying to Tuck (application deadlines)](https://www.tuck.dartmouth.edu/admissions/apply)\n- [Required curriculum](https://tuck.dartmouth.edu/mba/academic-experience/required-curriculum)\n- [Academic FAQs](https://tuck.dartmouth.edu/mba/academic-experience/academic-faqs)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
