    "title": "UCLA Anderson — MBA",
    "body": "# UCLA Anderson — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#18 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of California, Los Angeles\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUCLA Anderson Full-Time MBA: ~22 months with a ten-course core foundation, customizable electives, and a two-quarter Capstone Project.\n\nOrientation: ~22 months · 10-course core · Capstone\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$82,734 — Academic-year MBA program fees (Full-Time MBA, self-supporting); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUCLA Anderson Full-Time MBA Financing Estimated Financial Aid Budget for Academic Year 2026–2027 lists Estimated MBA Program Fees $82,734 (Summer 2026 $10,635 + Fall/Winter/Spring $24,033 each). UCLA Registrar Self-Supporting Degree Fees 2026–27 lists Management MBA new students $82,733/year (continuing $79,452) — $1 difference from Anderson’s quarterly sum; Anderson budget figure used. Self-supporting flat program fee (no resident/nonresident split). Mandatory UCLA fees $2,105 and health insurance $8,668 AY are separate; total mandatory charges $93,507; total estimated student budget $137,951. Full-time MBA only — not FEMBA/EMBA.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 6 Jan 2027 · 11:59 p.m. PT (Full-Time MBA; R1 passed). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — Test score not required. Applicants may submit GRE, GMAT, GMAT Focus, or EA, or opt out and instead submit a brief MBA-readiness essay showing quantitative/analytical prep (coursework, certifications, professional experience, expired scores). No minimum if submitting; highest total sitting used (no superscore). English proficiency optionality does NOT apply. GRE code 0771.\n- GMAT: optional — GMAT/GMAT Focus/EA optional under same flexible policy as GRE. Code 2NZ-2F-24. UCLA Law/Medicine concurrent students may use LSAT/MCAT respectively.\n- TOEFL: required — min 87 — UCLA Grad admission minimum TOEFL iBT 87 (before Jan 21 2026) or 4.5 (on/after Jan 21 2026). Anderson FAQ: almost all admits score over 100 iBT. Code 4837-02 for Anderson MBA. Valid within 2 years of application submission; not later than round deadline. Work experience in English does not waive.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS Academic overall 7.0 minimum (UCLA Grad). Anderson FAQ notes almost all admits ≥7.0. Send to Uni of California, Los Angeles-Anderson School of Management.\n- English waiver: Exempt with bachelor’s or higher from accredited U.S. university or from a country/institution where English is the sole language of instruction per WHED. Citizenship, U.S. residence, and work experience are not substitutes. Anderson emphasizes education in English—not work—as the key factor.\n- GPA: not_stated — Four-year bachelor’s or equivalent required to enroll; three-year undergrad may be admitted if profile strong. No numeric minimum GPA; do not convert non-4.0 scales.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two recommendations for new applicants (one new for reapplicants), preferably direct supervisor/manager in work setting. Online form with standard prompts.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Short essay prompts — Three short essays for 2026–2027: (1) short-/long-term goals + Anderson resources (250 words); (2) how classmates will describe you / values as leader (250); (3) first thing you’d tell classmates (50). Optional extenuating-circumstances essay (250). Test-optional applicants also submit MBA-readiness essay.\n- Resume: required — Résumé must be submitted; ideally one page, max two. Does not replace Employment section of application.\n- Transcripts: required — Scanned academic records with application; official hard copies only if invited to interview (upon request). International: multiple docs per International Students page + translations.\n- Interview: by_invitation — By invitation only after review; an interview must be completed to be admitted. Zoom or in person (~30 min), usually by trained second-year students; blind except résumé. All candidates being considered for admission are interviewed.\n- Fee: $200 — waivers: U.S. military applicants; current UCLA graduate students; SIEML program participants—upload docs in application; do not pay first (no refunds). — $200 online application fee. Applications for Class of 2029 noted as opening Aug 1, 2025 on requirements page.\n- Other: Rounds: Oct 1 2026 / Jan 6 2027 / Apr 7 2027 (decisions Dec 11 2026 / Mar 26 2027 / May 14 2027)\n- Other: Early career and college seniors may apply; most students have work experience\n- Other: Apply to only one Anderson program per year\n\nTest-optional ≠ English-optional. If skipping GMAT/GRE, invest in the readiness essay with quant evidence. Plan for interview if competitive—required to receive an offer.\n\n- [FT MBA Admissions hub](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba/admissions)\n- [Requirements](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba/admissions/requirements)\n- [Admissions FAQ (fee, English, interview)](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba/admissions/faq)\n- [UCLA Grad English requirements](https://grad.ucla.edu/admissions/english-requirements/)\n\n## Internships\n\nThe capstone provides hands-on client work; it is not itself a guaranteed paid internship.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-046, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Full-Time MBA academics](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba/academics)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba/financing)\n- [Registrar self-supporting fees 2026–27](https://registrar.ucla.edu/fees-residence/self-supporting-degrees)\n- [Full-Time MBA Admissions (rounds)](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba/admissions)\n- [Full-Time MBA Admissions FAQ (11:59 p.m. PT)](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba/admissions/faq)\n- [Full-Time MBA](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba/)\n- [Full-Time MBA](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba)\n- [Customizable schedule](https://www.anderson.ucla.edu/degrees/full-time-mba/academics/customizable-schedule)\n- [Grad Division MBA requirements](https://grad.ucla.edu/graduate-program-requirements/program-requirements-for-management-mba-6-2-2-2-2-2-2/)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
