    "path": "03-business/programs/utd-mba.md",
    "title": "UT Dallas Jindal — MBA",
    "body": "# UT Dallas Jindal — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#23 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Texas at Dallas\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUT Dallas Full-Time MBA Cohort: ~18–21 months, 53 hours (32 core + 21 electives), lock-step with pre-fall boot camp.\n\nOrientation: ~18–21 months · 53 hours · Cohort\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$36,532 — Academic-year tuition (Full-Time MBA, Nonresident; Fall I + Spring I); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUT Dallas MBA Cost & Tuition Plan 2026–2027 Estimated Variable Tuition (Full-Time MBA): Nonresident Cost $18,266 Fall I + $18,266 Spring I = $36,532 academic year (matches Bursar Non-Resident/Graduate Variable 2026–27 rate at 12+ SCH). Resident Cost $9,111/semester ($18,222 AY). Separate MBA/program Fees column $1,500 Fall I + $1,700 Spring I = $3,200 AY (MGT supplemental $100/SCH) not included in the $36,532. Published full-program Nonresident Tuition on 53 credits $60,307 + Fees $5,300 = $65,607 — full-duration totals, not used as the annual figure. School states all Full-Time admits get ≥$1,000 merit scholarship qualifying for resident rates; nonresident sticker used per OOS-primary rule. Full-time MBA only — not Professional/Online.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 8 Jan (month-day; year not labeled on official FT MBA deadlines table; fall start; R1 Oct 15 passed if same annual cycle). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — GRE accepted equally with GMAT Focus. Program is not test-optional. GRE school code R6897. Upload unofficial score; official required if admitted. Automatic waiver path for PhD/PharmD/DBA or U.S.-based MD/JD or MCAT/LSAT report; other waivers evaluated on Academic Readiness, Quantitative/Analytic Strength, Leadership/Professional Maturity, Supplemental Evidence (not guaranteed). Scholarship eligibility generally requires a submitted GMAT/GRE.\n- GMAT: required — GMAT Focus or GRE required (not test-optional). No strict minimum; FT MBA Class of 2023 average GMAT ~689 (650–700 mid range cited on admissions FAQ). GMAT codes via Jindal GMAC listing. Waiver paths same as GRE detail.\n- TOEFL: required — min 80 — International applicants must provide English proficiency. UT Dallas Graduate Admissions: TOEFL iBT min 80 (tests on/before 2026-01-26) or 4 (after 2026-01-26); PBT 550. School code 6897. Scores <2 years old at admission.\n- IELTS: required — min 6.5 — IELTS Academic minimum 6.5 (UT Dallas Graduate Admissions). DET min 105 and PTE Academic min 67 also accepted university-wide.\n- English waiver: Automatically waived if bachelor's/master's earned through instruction and examination in English; or native country primary language is English (UTD recognized list). MBA FAQ also cites U.S. bachelor's/master's and English-instruction degree.\n- GPA: required — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — UT Dallas Graduate Admissions expects overall GPA of 3.0 (4.0 scale) or better for graduate admission; MBA review is holistic.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 1 — One letter from a professional contact (need not be an employer). Submit via online LOR system or PDF to mba@utdallas.edu.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Statement of purpose; second essay — Statement of purpose plus a second essay (each 300–500 words) via applicant portal. Second essay prompts strategies for continued personal/professional success and 5/10/15-year vision after the FT MBA and how the program helps.\n- Resume: required — Detailed résumé of all work history required. Two years post-baccalaureate work experience required; exceptions considered for internship experience or strong academic record.\n- Transcripts: required — Upload official digital copies of transcripts from all universities attended (unofficial copies not accepted for review upload). If admitted, official transcripts sent directly from issuing university.\n- Interview: by_invitation — Interviews by invitation only for Full-Time MBA candidates.\n- Fee: $75 — waivers: Automatically waived for UT Dallas alumni, active-duty military, and veterans. — $75 for domestic and international candidates.\n- Other: Fall-only Full-Time MBA cohort (18-month). Incomplete files not reviewed.\n- Other: Rounds (month-day on table; years unlabeled on FT MBA page): Oct 15 / Jan 8 / Mar 1 / May 1 then rolling.\n- Other: MS/MBA dual path: apply to MS per MS rules; combining FT MBA cohort with MS occurs after MBA admission.\n- Other: Seat fee $750 within 10 days of admit (programming fee, not tuition deposit).\n\nGMAT/GRE required unless waiver granted—optional ≠ waived. Scholarship competition typically needs a test score. Use Grad Admissions English minima alongside MBA checklist.\n\n- [UT Dallas Full-Time MBA Admissions](https://mba.utdallas.edu/admissions/full-time-mba/)\n- [UT Dallas MBA Admissions FAQ](https://mba.utdallas.edu/admissions/)\n- [UT Dallas Graduate Admissions International Students (English)](https://graduate-admissions.utdallas.edu/apply-to-ut-dallas/international-students/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-057, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Full-Time MBA curriculum](https://mba.utdallas.edu/academics/full-time-mba/curriculum/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://mba.utdallas.edu/tuition-value/)\n- [Bursar tuition rates 2026–27](https://bursar.utdallas.edu/tuition/tuition-rates/)\n- [Full-Time MBA academics](https://mba.utdallas.edu/academics/full-time-mba/)\n- [Full-Time MBA Admissions (deadlines table)](https://mba.utdallas.edu/admissions/full-time-mba/)\n- [MBA programs hub](https://mba.utdallas.edu/)\n- [Catalog Business Administration](https://catalog.utdallas.edu/2026/graduate/programs/jsom/business-administration)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
