    "path": "03-business/programs/washington-mba.md",
    "title": "Washington Foster — MBA",
    "body": "# Washington Foster — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#20 in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: University of Washington\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nFoster Full-Time MBA: 2 years, 88 credits. Integrated Y1 core; customized Y2 electives; summer internship/project.\n\nOrientation: 2 years · 88 credits · Integrated core\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$60,180 — Academic-year tuition (Full-Time MBA, nonresident; 3 quarters); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nUW Foster Full-Time MBA Tuition and Financing: Non-resident $20,060 tuition per quarter + $403 fees; Resident $14,166 tuition + $403 fees. Academic-year (three-quarter) nonresident tuition = 3 × $20,060 = $60,180 (tuition+fees AY ≈ $61,389). Published Total Estimated Program Cost (six quarters / two years) is $122,778 nonresident / $87,414 resident — full-program totals, not used as the annual tuition field. Cohort rate held for both years once enrolled. Full-time MBA only.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 5 Jan 2027 · 11:59 p.m. PDT (Full-time MBA 2026–2027; R1 passed; final for internationals). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GRE optional; GMAT 10th Edition, GMAT Focus, or GRE encouraged. GRE code 4854. Highest overall single-attempt score used; GMAT Superscore not incorporated for 2027 cycle. Test Optional path requires 'Test Optional Summary of Qualifications' (150 words max on analytical/quantitative preparedness). Optional ≠ waived requirement—applicants may apply without scores.\n- GMAT: optional — GMAT optional (code 459-75-46 on requirements table; FAQ also lists 459-75-20—confirm live portal). EA not accepted for Full-time MBA. Test Optional available with short-answer evidence; internationals strongly encouraged to submit a score.\n- TOEFL: required — min 5 — If native language is not English: TOEFL minimum 5 (100 iBT for tests before Jan 21, 2026). Code 4854. Official scores required before offer; valid 2 years on application submit date.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS 7.0 or higher (code 365). Duolingo 130+ also accepted (University of Washington Graduate Admissions).\n- English waiver: Met via bachelor's/master's/doctoral degree from accredited institution with English as medium of instruction, subject to UW residency conditions for MOI degrees and documentation (except listed English-speaking countries). Living/working in U.S. alone does not satisfy. Requirement cannot be waived outside Policy 3.2 pathways.\n- GPA: recommended — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — No absolute minimum for Foster; GPA of 3.0 (B) or better is generally the standard for a competitive candidate. Report last 90 quarter / 60 semester graded credits on 4.0 scale per Grad School instructions. Below 3.0 reviewed holistically with test scores and other materials. UW Grad School Test Optional guidance also references ≥3.0 in most recent degree.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two recommendations required (up to three allowed). Preferably professional contacts. Short-answer questions plus written assessment (strengths, improvement areas, leadership, interpersonal skills, motivation, accomplishments).\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Required Essays (Post-MBA Plans; Foster Mission Statement) — Two required essays: (1) Post-MBA Plans 550–750 words; (2) Foster Mission Statement 350–550 words. Optional Essay (≤500 words) and Optional Nurturing Our Community Essay (350–550 words).\n- Resume: required — Reverse-chronological work experience; up to three pages allowed; include education, activities, community involvement since high school.\n- Transcripts: required — Upload scanned PDFs of original transcripts from completed four-year U.S. bachelor's (or equivalent) and other institutions attended. Include grading keys; English translation for non-English docs. Officials only after accepting offer.\n- Interview: by_invitation — Required video interview invitation emailed 1–3 business days after round deadline (~1 week to complete). Separate admissions interview by invitation only (Zoom), typically 3–5 weeks after deadline; must complete if invited to remain under consideration.\n- Fee: $90 — waivers: Foster does not offer program fee waivers; limited need-based waivers may be available via UW Graduate School. — Non-refundable $90 paid by credit card in online application.\n- Other: 2026–27 cycle: R1 Oct 1 2026; R2 Jan 5 2027 (final for internationals); R3 Mar 23 2027. One application per academic year; fall intake only.\n- Other: Consortium applicants supported; test optional available via Consortium as well.\n- Other: Disclose AI assistance per Foster Integrity Statement if used to refine (not create) essays.\n\nTest optional ≠ waived—still must complete Test Optional Summary. Round 2 is final international deadline. Official English scores must arrive by deadline.\n\n- [Foster Full-time MBA Admissions](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/admissions/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nMaster’s scholarship eligibility, award coverage and deadlines are not yet verified. Doctoral funding must not be assumed to cover this degree.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-047, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Full-time MBA curriculum](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/curriculum/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/tuition-and-fees/)\n- [Full-time MBA Admissions (2026–2027 deadlines)](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/admissions/)\n- [Full-time MBA](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/)\n- [Course descriptions](https://foster.uw.edu/academics/degree-programs/full-time-mba/course-descriptions/)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
