    "path": "03-business/programs/yale-mba.md",
    "title": "Yale SOM — MBA",
    "body": "# Yale SOM — MBA\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#11 (tie) in U.S. News Best Business Schools · full-time MBA, April 2026 release.\n\n30 schools occupy ranks 1–29; ties are retained. These are full-time MBA ranks, not business subject, online MBA or specialized master’s ranks.\n\nRanking provenance: [Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/). The publisher’s direct table was inaccessible; the position is secondary-source reported.\n\nUniversity: Yale University\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MBA\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nYale SOM MBA: 2 years, 72 units. Integrated Year-1 core (Orientation + Organizational Perspectives) then Year-2 electives; summer internship required.\n\nOrientation: 2 years · 72 units · Integrated core\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$90,900 — Academic-year tuition (Yale SOM MBA); 2026–27.\n\n2026–27 reference, not a Fall 2027 quote or full-degree total.\n\nYale SOM Affording Your MBA Cost Information lists Cost of Attendance 2026–27 with Tuition $90,900 and Program Fee $500 (Total Tuition and Fees $91,400). Living expenses, books, transportation, and Yale Health insurance ($3,764) are separate; total single-student budget $128,976. Joint-degree fees may differ.\n\nApplication timing: Round 2 · 6 Jan 2027 (Fall 2027 / 2026–27 cycle; R1 passed; clock time not on table). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — Verified GMAT or GRE required; Yale SOM does not waive the test score requirement for any applicant. GRE code 3986. Scores valid 5 years and must be valid on submit date; official report by Post-Submission Materials Deadline. Highest score credited; all reported scores considered. No minimum.\n- GMAT: required — GMAT (including online/newer shorter versions) required alternatively to GRE—no preference. Send to Yale School of Management MBA, Full-Time via mba.com. LSAT also accepted for law-school-path candidates (email mba.admissions@yale.edu for instructions). No waivers.\n- TOEFL: not_required — TOEFL not required for international MBA applicants. Fluency in English required for admission; assessed in part via video questions.\n- IELTS: not_required — IELTS and PTE Academic not required for international MBA applicants.\n- English waiver: N/A—English proficiency exams are not required; video questions help assess communication/English skills.\n- GPA: not_stated — No minimum GPA stated. Report GPA only if listed on transcript; otherwise leave blank and check 'No GPA reported on transcript.' Class Profile has ranges.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two professional recommendations; ideally one from most recent supervisor. Silver Scholars: one academic + one professional. Letters in English (translation OK).\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Essay; video questions; Behavioral Assessment — Choose one of three essay prompts (500-word limit): biggest commitment; most meaningful community; or most significant challenge. Optional Information section truly optional. After submit + fee: video questions (two recorded prompts, 60 seconds each) and ETS Behavioral Assessment (~25 minutes).\n- Resume: required — Resume required; typically one page unless >10 years experience. Focus on accomplishments/impact.\n- Transcripts: required — Transcripts from every college/university attended (undergrad, graduate, study abroad, transfer, non-degree for credit). Unofficial OK to apply; official if enroll. Non-English: original + notarized English translation. Three-year international degrees may apply.\n- Interview: by_invitation — All admitted applicants will have had an interview. Invitations rolling within round; 30-minute blind interview with 2Y student, recent alum, or Admissions. Waitlisted candidates may interview later rounds.\n- Fee: $250 — waivers: Sliding scale: $175 if earning <$50k/year; $125 if <$25k/year (based on reported compensation; verified if enroll). Full waivers: U.S. military/veterans; alumni/students of ~700 economic-diversity U.S. colleges (≥35% Pell); Girls Who Invest alumni; Forté MBALaunch; Peace Corps; current Yale students; MLT MBA Prep Fellows; Teach for America/China/India/Teach for All; QuestBridge seniors/alumni. Request ≥48 hours before deadline. — Standard fee $250 with income-based sliding scale.\n- Other: 2026–27 deadlines: R1 Sep 15 2026; R2 Jan 6 2027; R3 Apr 7 2027.\n- Other: Consortium and QuestBridge Graduate School Match pathways available.\n- Other: Silver Scholars Program for college seniors (same application with recommender differences).\n- Other: Full-time work experience strongly encouraged but not required (avg ~5 years).\n\nGMAT/GRE required with no waivers—do not treat as optional. No TOEFL/IELTS needed. Complete video questions and Behavioral Assessment promptly after fee payment.\n\n- [Yale SOM MBA Application Information](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information)\n- [Yale SOM MBA Application Guide](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide)\n- [Yale SOM MBA Admissions FAQ](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/faq)\n- [Yale SOM International Students](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/international-students)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nAll full-time MBA students complete Scholarship Application after admission for Yale SOM scholarships; international students eligible for school scholarships (country-specific awards also exist). Median award figure is Class of 2027 statistic, not a guarantee.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-005, SCH-015, SCH-017, SCH-019, SCH-020, SCH-034, SCH-035, SCH-036, SCH-037, SCH-038, SCH-062, SCH-064, SCH-072, SCH-074, SCH-082, SCH-084. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Integrated curriculum](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/curriculum)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/affording-your-mba/cost-information)\n- [Affording Your MBA](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/affording-your-mba)\n- [MBA Application Information (deadlines)](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information)\n- [MBA Admissions](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions)\n- [MBA program](https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba)\n- [MBA curriculum (catalog)](https://catalog.yale.edu/management/full-time-mba/mba-curriculum/)\n- [Core courses](https://catalog.yale.edu/management/courses/mba-core-courses/)\n- [U.S. News positions via Clear Admit](https://www.clearadmit.com/mba-rankings/usnews/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
