    "body": "# Arizona Eller — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#30 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of Arizona\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nArizona Eller MSF: STEM, 30 cr, ~9 mo Tucson. Deadlines Oct 15 early / May 15 intl / Jun 1 FINPREP / Aug 1 final (years for F27). Tuition NR $47,500 / AZ $27,200 (2026–27).\n\nOrientation: Fall · ~9 months · STEM · TFE #30 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$47,500 — Non-resident tuition — Tucson on-campus MS Finance 9-month / 30 units (Eller Matrix 2026–27); 2026–27 (Eller graduate programs matrix PDF dated Aug 2026).\n\nSTEM; ~9 months Tucson on-campus; 30 units. Open external/intl. Prefer matrix sticker ($47,500 NR / $27,200 AZ) as official 2026–27 program matrix; ROI page itemization differs by ~$78. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nAlternate format: Arizona resident tuition — 9-month Tucson MSF (2026–27 matrix) $27,200. Matrix footnote: tuition and fees subject to change. ROI page itemizes AZ resident 9-mo total $27,122 and Non-AZ $47,422 (slightly below matrix round numbers) including program fees/fees lines; $500 seat fee due after admission applied toward tuition if student attends. FINPrep non-credit summer module $2,500 separate if required. Online MSF listed separately $37,500 ($1,250/unit) — different modality. STEM; ~9 months Tucson on-campus; 30 units. Open external/intl. Prefer matrix sticker ($47,500 NR / $27,200 AZ) as official 2026–27 program matrix; ROI page itemization differs by ~$78.\n\nApplication timing: Fall Early Admission · 2026-10-15 · Bullet list used; same page also mentions Dec 1 preferred intl / Feb 1 — confirm. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: waived — GMAT/GRE requirement waived for Fall 2027 (stated on admissions page Application Strengths and Required Materials). Historical note on page also describes alternate waiver paths (Finance/Accounting/STEM degree with ≥3.3 GPA, CFA levels, Charter)—but Fall 2027 policy is explicit waiver.\n- GMAT: waived — GMAT (or GRE) waived Fall 2027. School code 4832 if somehow submitting. Page still mentions older waiver alternatives; treat Fall 2027 as waived.\n- TOEFL: required — min 100 — International / non-native: Eller FAQ requires iBT TOEFL ≥100. Score <2 years old at first MSF class unless living/studying in U.S. since test. Code 4832.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS overall ≥7.0 with ≥6.0 each section (Eller FAQ / UA Grad College).\n- English waiver: Waived if completed a four-year bachelor’s from a U.S. college/university and have not returned home for an extended period (FAQ); also if completed a degree program in the U.S. Check country requirements on UA Graduate College site.\n- GPA: required — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — Minimum GPA 3.00. UA Grad College enforces ≥3.0 on last 60 undergrad units or 12 grad credits (rare exception >2.95 with strong credentials).\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — 2 Letters of Reference: names and contact information. Academia or industry; should address study/quantitative skills.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Statement of Purpose — Statement of Purpose: academic/professional goals in finance; typically 1–2 typed double-spaced pages to Finance Department Admissions Committee.\n- Resume: required — Resume required in application package.\n- Transcripts: required — Transcripts from all colleges/universities except UA (include grade key if not 4.0 scale). International: original language + English translation; official sealed.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not listed among Required Application Materials.\n- Fee: $90 — waivers: UA Graduate College does not waive application fees (general email requests not considered). — UA Graduate College degree-seeking application fee $90 nonrefundable.\n- Other: No work experience required.\n- Other: Prefer B.S./B.A. in business-related field; other fields may need summer FinPrep/prereq modules.\n- Other: International: financial guarantee; affidavit of domicile for AZ residents.\n- Other: Fall deadlines include Oct 15 early; May 15 international; Aug 1 final.\n\nFall 2027 GMAT/GRE waived—do not delay for a test. Non-finance majors should plan FinPrep if notified.\n\n- [MSF admissions](https://eller.arizona.edu/programs/masters/finance/ms-finance/admissions)\n- [MSF FAQs (English / GPA)](https://eller.arizona.edu/programs/masters/finance/ms-finance/faqs)\n- [UA Grad application fees](https://grad.arizona.edu/admissions/procedures/application-fees)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-125.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-125. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program hub / STEM](https://eller.arizona.edu/programs/masters/finance/ms-finance)\n- [Admissions / deadlines](https://eller.arizona.edu/programs/masters/finance/ms-finance/admissions)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://eller.arizona.edu/sites/default/files/2026-08/Matrix-2026-2027.pdf)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [Eller MSF Cost / ROI](https://eller.arizona.edu/programs/masters/finance/ms-finance/roi)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
