    "body": "# ASU W. P. Carey — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#12 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Arizona State University\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance (MS-FIN)\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nASU Carey MS-FIN: STEM; Aug start; 9–16 months. Fall 2027: Dec 1 / Feb 1 (intl priority) / Apr 1 (intl final) / Jul 1 (+ rolling to Jul 15). Est. intl tuition+fees Corporate ~$73,500 / Analytical ~$99,500.\n\nOrientation: Fall (Aug) · 9–16 months · STEM · TFE #12 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$73,500 — MS-FIN Corporate finance track — estimated total tuition and fees, International; 2026–27 · as published on W. P. Carey MS-FIN cost page (Fall 2027 cycle; subject to ABOR change).\n\nSTEM. Starts August; length 9–16 months (Corporate vs Analytical methods). Resident / Nonresident / International estimates: Corporate $43,500 / $70,000 / $73,500; Analytical $61,500 / $95,000 / $99,500. Same figures on main program page as of asOf. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nAlternate format: MS-FIN Analytical methods track — estimated total tuition and fees, International $99,500. Mandatory fees reference: $500. One-time non-refundable enrollment deposit $500 required before registration (in addition to estimated totals as published). Estimated totals are labeled tuition and fees combined. STEM. Starts August; length 9–16 months (Corporate vs Analytical methods). Resident / Nonresident / International estimates: Corporate $43,500 / $70,000 / $73,500; Analytical $61,500 / $95,000 / $99,500. Same figures on main program page as of asOf.\n\nApplication timing: Round I (Early Decision) · 2026-12-01. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — Test scores not required for admission. Applicants may submit GRE to demonstrate potential; ASU does not accept GRE General Test at-home exam. Institution code 4007.\n- GMAT: optional — Test scores not required. Optional GMAT may be submitted; W. P. Carey GMAT code 0GZ-1R-80.\n- TOEFL: required — min 80 — Required for non-native English speakers. ASU graduate minimum: TOEFL iBT 80 if taken before Jan 21, 2026; minimum 4 on new scale if on/after Jan 21, 2026. W. P. Carey states its graduate minimums may be higher than ASU but does not publish a program-specific number on the MS-FIN page. Does not accept TOEFL iBT Home Edition if taken prior to Jan 21, 2026, Paper Edition, or Essentials.\n- IELTS: required — min 6.5 — IELTS Academic overall band at least 6.5 (ASU graduate minimum). W. P. Carey may set higher unpublished program minimums.\n- English waiver: ASU English proficiency exemptions (citizenship list, U.S. degree, medium-of-instruction, etc.) via Admission Services forms after applying. See admission.asu.edu English proficiency page.\n- GPA: required — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — ASU Degree Search: minimum cumulative GPA of 3.00 in last 60 semester / 90 quarter hours of first bachelor's, or 3.00 in applicable master's.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 1 — One letter of recommendation; provide recommender name, affiliation, and work email. Should comment on motivation, commitment, achievements, work experience, and likely success (Degree Search).\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Admission essay / short-answer question responses — Admission essay / short-answer question responses in graduate application. Personal statements will not be accepted and will delay review. Essay prompts are in the graduate application.\n- Resume: required — Current resume must include positions held and clearly indicate dates of employment in Month/Year format.\n- Transcripts: required — Unofficial OK at application; if admitted, official transcripts from every college/university awarding bachelor's or higher required. ASU attendees need not submit ASU transcripts. International: original language + official English translation.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not mentioned on MS-FIN application-process page.\n- Fee: $115 — waivers: Military and Citizen Service: U.S. Military, Teach for America, Peace Corps, or AmeriCorps — email wpcareymasters@asu.edu before applying. Domestic fee $70. — $70 domestic; $115 international. Non-refundable; applications not processed until fee received.\n- Other: Bachelor's or master's from regionally accredited institution in business/management, economics, statistics, CS, or other STEM areas (Degree Search).\n- Other: Three-year undergraduate degree with no additional coursework may qualify — contact wpcareymasters@asu.edu.\n- Other: $500 non-refundable enrollment deposit after admission.\n\nInternational priority Round II Feb 1, 2027; international final Round III Apr 1, 2027. Submit English proof and allow visa/financial guarantee time after admission.\n\n- [MS-FIN application process](https://www.wpcarey.asu.edu/masters-programs/finance/application-process)\n- [MS-FIN program hub](https://wpcarey.asu.edu/masters-programs/finance)\n- [ASU Degree Search Finance MS](https://degrees.asu.edu/masters-phd/major/ASU00/BAFINMS/finance-ms/)\n- [ASU graduate English proficiency](https://admission.asu.edu/apply/international/graduate/english-proficiency)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-099. MBA-only merit (SCH-031) is not attached to this MSF route.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-099. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program / cost / deadlines](https://wpcarey.asu.edu/masters-programs/finance)\n- [Application process](https://www.wpcarey.asu.edu/masters-programs/finance/application-process)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://wpcarey.asu.edu/masters-programs/finance/cost-financial-aid)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
