    "title": "Auburn Harbert — MSF",
    "body": "# Auburn Harbert — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#23 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Auburn University\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nAuburn Harbert MSF: fall only; 30–31 cr; STEM not stated. Deadlines Apr 1 intl / Jun 1 dom (years for entry year). Tuition per-credit 2026–27 $643 AL / $1,975 NR + $241/cr professional — no flat total.\n\nOrientation: Fall only · 30–31 cr · STEM unstated · TFE #23 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\nNot verified — Tuition not yet verified; 2026–27 per-credit / fee schedule (no flat MSF sticker).\n\nOpen Fall-only on-campus admits (also online modality). Bulletin non-thesis = 30 hours (admissions page text said 31 — use bulletin/curriculum 30). No published flat program tuition. Resident estimate 2 × ($643 × 9) = $11,574 tuition + same professional/services structure. Financial assistance page points to loans via Office of Financial Aid — no verified open applicant-facing merit SCH amounts. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nEstimate only: non-resident graduate tuition for 30-credit non-thesis MSF assuming two semesters at ≥9 credits each — 2 × ($1,975 × 9) = $35,550. NOT a published flat program sticker.: $35,550. Estimate components (2026–27): College of Business Graduate professional fee $241/credit × 30 = $7,230; Student Services Fee $1,002 × 2 semesters = $2,004; Confirmation Fee $450 one-time; Graduation Fee $40 one-time → ≈ $9,724. Actual semester count / credit load changes fees. Alabama resident credit tuition $643/cr (capped at 9 hrs). Open Fall-only on-campus admits (also online modality). Bulletin non-thesis = 30 hours (admissions page text said 31 — use bulletin/curriculum 30). No published flat program tuition. Resident estimate 2 × ($643 × 9) = $11,574 tuition + same professional/services structure. Financial assistance page points to loans via Office of Financial Aid — no verified open applicant-facing merit SCH amounts.\n\nApplication timing: Fall — International · April 1 (year not labeled on table — use April 1 of entry year, e.g. 2027-04-01 for Fall 2027). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — Official GMAT (preferred) or GRE required unless waiver granted. Waiver: bachelor’s from regionally accredited institution plus (2+ yrs exp & 3.50+ GPA) OR (4+ yrs & 3.25+) OR (6+ yrs & 3.0+) OR (8+ yrs) OR terminal degree. Case-by-case additional waivers. Waiver ≠ admission.\n- GMAT: required — Official GMAT preferred or GRE, unless waiver (same criteria as GRE). Online waiver request available; advisor appointment advised.\n- TOEFL: required — min 79 — International: TOEFL iBT 79+ with ≥16 each section (pre-Jan 21, 2026); after Jan 21, 2026 iBT26 total 4.5+ with ≥4.0 each section. ETS code 1005. DET also accepted (115+ with 110+ sections).\n- IELTS: required — min 6.5 — IELTS overall band 6.5 or higher.\n- English waiver: Prior degree from regionally accredited U.S. institution may remove English score requirement once official transcript with degree received; other exemptions case-by-case after official transcript.\n- GPA: recommended — minimum 2.75 — scale 4.0 — MSF program page states bachelor’s required but no program-specific GPA floor. Auburn Graduate School typically expects ≥2.75 undergrad GPA (or ≥3.0 grad GPA or acceptable GRE/GMAT). Competitive admission; class size limited.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two letters of recommendation on checklist.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Personal Statement — Personal Statement required on application checklist.\n- Resume: required — Résumé required.\n- Transcripts: required — Official undergraduate university transcript(s). International: original language + certified English translation; diploma/certificate.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not listed on MS Finance admissions checklist.\n- Fee: $60 — waivers: Active military: Graduate School application fee waiver with confirmation letter. International pay $70. — Graduate School: $60 domestic / $70 international (nonrefundable), paid online with application.\n- Other: Bachelor’s from recognized university/college required.\n- Other: Apply via Graduate School as Finance (Non-Thesis); fall admit only; 31 credit hours non-thesis.\n- Other: Duolingo English Test accepted for internationals.\n\nIf seeking GMAT/GRE waiver, schedule admissions advisor appointment before submitting waiver. International deadline earlier (Apr 1) than domestic (Jun 1).\n\n- [MS Finance admissions](https://harbert.auburn.edu/degrees-programs/graduate/ms-finance/admissions.html)\n- [Graduate School international instructions](https://graduate.auburn.edu/admissions/international-instructions.php)\n- [Graduate School bulletin admissions](https://bulletin.auburn.edu/thegraduateschool/admissions/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nNo verified open applicant-facing merit scholarship for auburn-msf (as of 2026-10-26). Loans pointer only; no SCH card.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: No verified award links yet. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program hub](https://harbert.auburn.edu/degrees-programs/graduate/ms-finance/)\n- [Admissions / deadlines / 31 cr](https://harbert.auburn.edu/degrees-programs/graduate/ms-finance/admissions.html)\n- [Curriculum / 30 cr](https://harbert.auburn.edu/degrees-programs/graduate/ms-finance/curriculum.html)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://harbert.auburn.edu/degrees-programs/graduate/ms-finance/tuition-financial-assistance.html)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [Auburn Bulletin Basic Charges (eff. Fall 2026)](https://bulletin.auburn.edu/generalinformation/financialinformation/basicchargesrevisedmay/)\n- [Auburn Bulletin MS Finance](https://bulletin.auburn.edu/thegraduateschool/graduatedegreesoffered/finance_ms/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
