    "path": "05-finance/programs/bc-msf.md",
    "title": "Boston College Carroll — MSF",
    "body": "# Boston College Carroll — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#17 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Boston College\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nBC Carroll MSF: 10 courses/~12 mo FT. Quant STEM (Fall Aug or Spring Jan); Regular Fall only. Fall 2027 rounds Oct 13’26–Jun 8’27; Spring Quant final Dec 15’26. Tuition 2026–27 $71,940 ($2,398/cr × 30).\n\nOrientation: Fall (Aug) or Spring Quant · ~12 months · Quant STEM · TFE #17 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$71,940 — Carroll MSF program total — 30 credits × $2,398/credit (2026–27 AY); 2026–27 (rates typically announced in April; effective summer start of AY).\n\nFull-time MSF: 10 courses / 30 credits / ~12 months. Regular Finance track Fall (Aug) entry only; Quantitative Finance track is STEM-designated and offers Fall Aug 2027 and Spring Jan 2027 entry. Same published per-credit tuition applies to both tracks; merit funding page does not limit awards to STEM/Quant track. Fall 2027 students will be billed on the AY rate in force when enrolled (2027–28 rates typically announced April 2027 — not published as of asOf; 2026–27 used as current published schedule).\n\nMandatory fees reference: $196. Graduate Student Activity Fee $73/semester × 2 (Fall+Spring, 7+ credits) + Initial BC ID Card $50 = $196. Summer term with <7 credits may add $42 activity fee (not assumed). Medical Insurance $4,723 (Fall $2,083 + Spring $2,604) separate / waivable with comparable coverage. Full-time MSF: 10 courses / 30 credits / ~12 months. Regular Finance track Fall (Aug) entry only; Quantitative Finance track is STEM-designated and offers Fall Aug 2027 and Spring Jan 2027 entry. Same published per-credit tuition applies to both tracks; merit funding page does not limit awards to STEM/Quant track. Fall 2027 students will be billed on the AY rate in force when enrolled (2027–28 rates typically announced April 2027 — not published as of asOf; 2026–27 used as current published schedule). Living cost band from official COA: $28,928 (Carroll Tuition & Aid 2026–27 nine-month estimates: Housing $17,204 + Food $5,973 + Transportation $1,800 + Personal $2,651 + Books and Supplies $1,300 = $28,928 (excludes medical insurance).).\n\nApplication timing: Fall 2027 — Round 1 · 2026-10-13. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — Applicants must submit GMAT or GRE from within past five years. Full-time and part-time MSF applicants may request GMAT/GRE waiver consideration before completing application. GRE school code 3033. Class profile Fall 2026 avg GRE 319 (context only).\n- GMAT: required — GMAT Exam or GMAT Focus accepted. School code 44x-J5-96. Waiver request available for FT and PT MSF. No preference between GMAT/GRE. Fall 2026 FT avg GMAT Focus 644 (context).\n- TOEFL: required — min 100 — Non-U.S. citizens/PRs: TOEFL iBT traditional minimum 100; TOEFL iBT (New) minimum 5. Scores within past two years. MyBest not accepted.\n- IELTS: required — min 7.5 — IELTS minimum 7.5. Also PTE 68; Duolingo 130.\n- English waiver: Completed four-year bachelor's or two-year master's (or higher) entirely at English-medium institution (MOI on transcript or official letter); OR ≥2 years full-time post-degree work in U.S. or country where English is official language. No separate waiver form required if eligible.\n- GPA: not_stated — No minimum GPA required (FAQ). Fall 2026 FT average undergrad GPA 3.58 (profile).\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 1 — One required; up to three accepted. Academic (professors) or professional (supervisors/managers). Online recommendation forms.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Required essay — Required essay ≤500 words: past experiences, short- and long-term goals, why MSF at Boston College. Optional essay for uncovered aspects.\n- Resume: required — Resume or CV outlining education and professional experience including part-time/internships with months and years; recommend 1–2 pages.\n- Transcripts: required — Four-year bachelor's (or equivalent) required. Self-reported transcript at application; official if admitted. Non-U.S.: English translation + third-party degree verification (SpanTran/TEC or WES) if admitted.\n- Interview: not_used — MSF application materials page does not list an interview. FAQ interview-by-invitation applies to Ph.D. programs, not MSF.\n- Fee: $100 — waivers: Reapplicants: contact Graduate Admissions before submitting for fee waiver (FAQ). — Nonrefundable $100 USD.\n- Other: Quantitative Finance STEM track selected on enrollment form after admission (not separate application).\n- Other: Spring 2027 entry available for Quantitative Track only.\n- Other: Fifth-year BC undergrad pathway exists with separate requirements page.\n\nInternational applicants strongly encouraged to apply by starred early deadlines for visa. Part-time not F-1 sponsored. Quant track STEM OPT extension path.\n\n- [MS in Finance (application & requirements)](https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/schools/carroll-school/graduate/ms-programs/ms-in-finance.html)\n- [Graduate Admission FAQ](https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/schools/carroll-school/graduate/admission/graduate-admission-faq.html)\n- [Admission deadlines hub](https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/schools/carroll-school/graduate/admission.html)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-107.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-107. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MSF program / curriculum / deadlines](https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/schools/carroll-school/graduate/ms-programs/ms-in-finance.html)\n- [Admission deadlines hub](https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/schools/carroll-school/graduate/admission.html)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/schools/carroll-school/graduate/admission/tuition-and-aid.html)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [BC Student Services Tuition & Fees](https://www.bc.edu/offices/student-services/billing-student-accounts/tuition-fees.html)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
