    "body": "# Claremont Graduate (Drucker) — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#18 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Claremont Graduate University\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nCGU Drucker MSF: STEM, 32 units/~1 yr. Spring/Fall primary starts. Fall 2027 priority Feb 1 / intl final Jun 1 / dom Aug 1. Est. tuition 32×$2,070=$66,240 (2025–26 rates).\n\nOrientation: Fall/Spring (+ summer TBD) · ~1 year · STEM · TFE #18 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$66,240 — Estimated program tuition — 32 units × $2,070/unit (2025–26 published rate; 2026–27 rate not posted as of asOf); 2026–27 · 2025–26 unit rate on program page (covers Summer 2025–Spring 2026). Fall 2027 intake will use later AY rates — not locked..\n\nSUMMER START. Drucker School MS in Finance; STEM; 32 units; ~1 year full-time; starts Spring, Summer, or Fall (Fall 2027 classes begin Aug 30, 2027). Same per-unit rate for CA resident / nonresident / international. Tuition figure is 32×$2,070 using 2025–26 published rate marked on program page — do not treat as locked Fall 2027 sticker.\n\nMandatory fees reference: $2,490. Student Fee $245 + Technology Fee $150 = $395/semester × 2 semesters = $790. International Student Services Fee (F-1): $802 fall + $898 spring = $1,700 (2025–26; covers annual accident/sickness plan + admin). Total fees shown $2,490 for two-semester full-time path. 2026–27 fees not separately published as of asOf. Drucker School MS in Finance; STEM; 32 units; ~1 year full-time; starts Spring, Summer, or Fall (Fall 2027 classes begin Aug 30, 2027). Same per-unit rate for CA resident / nonresident / international. Tuition figure is 32×$2,070 using 2025–26 published rate marked on program page — do not treat as locked Fall 2027 sticker. Living cost band from official COA: $25,000 (CGU International Students Estimated Annual Cost of Attendance (affidavit PDF, revised 2/2026): Living Expenses $25,000 for CGU Programs. Financial Aid COA 2025–26 also budgets Housing $12,500 + Personal $2,500 + Transportation $2,500 per semester for full unit loads.). SUMMER START — matriculation is not a standard autumn-only Fall intake.\n\nApplication timing: Fall 2027 — Priority · 2027-02-01. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — GRE or GMAT required (waivers available). Scores within past five years. ETS/GRE code 4053. Waiver paths include business bachelor's from AACSB/EQUIS school; BS in finance/accounting/business analytics/STEM; ≥4 units stats/calculus B+ or better; certain professional licenses; 5+ years quantitative work; partner-institution alumni — email admissions@cgu.edu when application started.\n- GMAT: required — GMAT or GRE required with same waiver policy. GMAT code DZK-QS-08.\n- TOEFL: required — min 95 — Non-native English speakers: TOEFL minimum 95 (old scale) / 5 (new score scale) for direct entry. Code 4053. Lower scores may enter via International Scholars Program (TOEFL 75/4).\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS 7.0 with no sub-score less than 6.5 for direct entry. Also PTE 66; Duolingo 125 for direct entry.\n- English waiver: Citizens/PRs of English sole-official-language countries; degree from U.S. or those countries; recent U.S. academic English pre-master's/bridge; or degree where English is a primary language of instruction for majority of courses with documentation.\n- GPA: not_stated — No GPA minimum published on MSF page or Drucker 2027 how-to-apply news (Associate Dean: no score cutoffs / no GPA minimums).\n- Letters of recommendation: optional — Optional. If submitting, recommender emails letter to admissions@cgu.edu with applicant full name. News post: no longer required.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Applicant questionnaire — Applicant questionnaire: five short responses ≤100 words each (motivation; goals; alignment with Drucker ideals; contribution; biggest challenge). Upload to status page after online application.\n- Resume: required — Up-to-date resume required.\n- Transcripts: required — Sealed official transcript from every undergrad/grad institution that granted a degree; electronic to admissions@cgu.edu OK. Unofficial for review; official upon admission. Bachelor's from regionally accredited college required.\n- Interview: required — Required for admission upon review of application; decision not issued until interview complete. Drucker news: every applicant who completes an application is interviewed.\n- Fee: $80 — $80 non-refundable (university requirements on MSF page).\n- Other: Prerequisite: Financial Accounting (coursework B or better at accredited institution or approved equivalent) before entering.\n- Other: Fall 2027: priority Feb 1, 2027; international final June 1, 2027 (program page) / June 5, 2027 (Drucker news table — slight date conflict; verify closer to cycle).\n- Other: STEM designated.\n\nInternational final deadline earlier than domestic for visa. Reach out to Drucker recruiters early; interview is mandatory after complete file.\n\n- [MS Finance program / application guidelines](https://www.cgu.edu/academics/program/ms-finance/)\n- [Drucker 2027 deadlines how to apply](https://www.cgu.edu/news/2026/08/drucker-school-application-deadlines-for-2027-how-to-apply/)\n- [CGU International Applicants (English mins)](https://www.cgu.edu/admissions/international-applicants/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-109.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-109. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.cgu.edu/academics/program/ms-finance/)\n- [Drucker 2027 deadlines news (apps open)](https://www.cgu.edu/news/2026/08/drucker-school-application-deadlines-for-2027-how-to-apply/)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [CGU Tuition & Fees](https://www.cgu.edu/admissions/cost-aid/tuition-fees/)\n- [CGU Financial Aid & Fellowships](https://www.cgu.edu/admissions/cost-aid/financial-aid-fellowships/)\n- [CGU Intl Cost of Attendance / Affidavit (rev 2/2026)](https://my.cgu.edu/international-services/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/02/CGU-International-Students-Cost-of-Attendance_2026.pdf)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
