    "body": "# University of Chicago (Physical Sciences / Math) — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#7 in QuantNet 2026 Ranking of Best Financial Engineering Programs (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nSeparate quant-mfe track. Not a TFE Times MSF rank. tfeRank2026 is null on every row. Stanford ICME MCF is not on the 2026 QuantNet list (QuantNet rank null).\n\nRanking provenance: [IBKR Quant News](https://www.interactivebrokers.com/campus/ibkr-quant-news/2026-quantnet-ranking-of-best-financial-engineering-programs/).\n\nUniversity: University of Chicago\n\nDegree route: MS in Financial Mathematics (MSFM)\n\nApplication status: Autumn 2027 (in-person); online also Jan 2027 / June 2027\n\n## Academic direction\n\nChicago MSFM: Autumn'27 R1 Nov 2'26 / R2 Feb 1'27. $8,017/100 units; 1,250 units. STEM. QuantNet #7.\n\nOrientation: Autumn (in-person) · ~5 quarters · QuantNet #7 · SEPARATE TRACK\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$100,213 — Illustrative program tuition if 1,250 units × ($8,017 / 100 units) 2026–27 in-person — unit total from brief/curriculum; confirm exact unit load; 2026–27.\n\nSEPARATE TRACK quant-mfe. In-person Autumn start; online also January/June. STEM. Enrollment deposit $3,000 credited to first Autumn tuition. Bursar PSD confirms FinMath In-Person 100 units = $8,017. Flat sticker only if unit total known — 1,250 u illustrative from brief (null if curriculum unit total changes). Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nPublished in-person rate: $8,017 per 100 units. Catalog tuition $100,213 is illustrative at 1,250 units, not a locked flat sticker if the unit load changes. Quarterly Student Services Fee $520; Student Insurance 2026 $1,839/qtr if USHIP; one-time lifetime transcript fee $84 first quarter. Exact fee total depends on number of quarters enrolled (~5 qtr typical in-person). Do not invent multi-quarter fee sum beyond published per-quarter amounts. SEPARATE TRACK quant-mfe. In-person Autumn start; online also January/June. STEM. Enrollment deposit $3,000 credited to first Autumn tuition. Bursar PSD confirms FinMath In-Person 100 units = $8,017. Flat sticker only if unit total known — 1,250 u illustrative from brief (null if curriculum unit total changes). Official: $8,017 per 100 units for 2026–27; degree requires 1,250 units (250 core + 100 computing + 900 elective). Quarterly Student Services Fee $520; USHIP 2026 $1,839 if enrolled; one-time transcript fee $84. Enrollment deposit $3,000 credited to first Autumn tuition. Living cost band not published for this program (null, not zero).\n\nApplication timing: In-person Autumn 2027 Round 1 · 2026-11-02. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GRE not required; welcome to enhance application. Self-report then official ETS (institution 1832; dept 0799 Mathematical Science–Other). Valid if exam within 5 years of deadline.\n- GMAT: not_accepted — Do not submit GMAT scores (or high school transcripts, theses, publications)—not considered.\n- TOEFL: required — min 90 — TOEFL iBT or IELTS Academic required unless exception. PSD policy minimum TOEFL 90 or IELTS 7; FinMath prefers significantly higher. Exams within 2 years of deadline. TOEFL code 1832 / dept 72.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS Academic (not General Training) accepted; minimum 7 per PSD policy.\n- English waiver: Waived if (a) English primary language of communication/schooling since childhood; OR (b) ≥1 academic year full-time at accredited English-medium post-secondary in listed countries/territories within past 10 years (incl. Antigua, Australia, Bahamas, Barbados, Canada, Dominica, Grenada, Guyana, Hong Kong, Ireland, Jamaica, NZ, St. Kitts/Nevis, St. Lucia, St. Vincent, Singapore, South Africa, Trinidad & Tobago, UK, USA). English-medium elsewhere / high school / part-time-research-only do not qualify.\n- GPA: not_stated — No minimum GPA stated on application-requirements page.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 3 — Three letters; at least one professional reference.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as candidate statements — Three candidate statements ≤250 words each (shortcoming/steps; program-city-career alignment; additional profile info).\n- Resume: required — Resume/CV with entire work history including start/end dates, locations, full- vs part-time.\n- Transcripts: required — Transcripts from all previous colleges/universities. Unofficial uploads for review; official final with degree conferral before enrollment if admitted.\n- Interview: not_used — No live interview listed among required documents. Two video statements are required application components (not a live interview).\n- Fee: $90 — waivers: Not stated on Apply page. — $90 per application submitted (Apply page).\n- Other: Two video statements required.\n- Other: Math prereqs: multivariable calculus, linear algebra, probability; programming ideally C++/Python/OOP.\n- Other: Work experience encouraged but not required.\n- Other: In-person Autumn 2027 rounds: Nov 2 2026; Feb 1 2027. Online also January/June starts.\n\nIn-person is Autumn start; online has Jan/June starts. GMAT not accepted. GRE optional.\n\n- [Application requirements](https://finmath.uchicago.edu/admissions/application-requirements/)\n- [Apply / deadlines / fee](https://finmath.uchicago.edu/admissions/apply/)\n- [Admission FAQ](https://finmath.uchicago.edu/admissions/admission-faq/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-145.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-145. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Apply / deadlines](https://finmath.uchicago.edu/admissions/apply/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://finmath.uchicago.edu/admissions/tuition/)\n- [Curriculum / 1250 units](https://finmath.uchicago.edu/page/curriculum)\n- [International / STEM OPT](https://finmath.uchicago.edu/admissions/international-students/)\n- [QuantNet 2026 MFE ranking via IBKR Quant News](https://www.interactivebrokers.com/campus/ibkr-quant-news/2026-quantnet-ranking-of-best-financial-engineering-programs/)\n- [UChicago Bursar PSD 2026–27 FinMath rates](https://bursar.uchicago.edu/Tuition-and-Fees/Tuition-and-Fees-2026-27/Tuition-and-Fees-2026-27-Physical-Sciences-Division)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
