    "path": "05-finance/programs/florida-msf.md",
    "title": "Florida Warrington — MSF",
    "body": "# Florida Warrington — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#11 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of Florida\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance (UF combination)\n\nApplication status: UF undergrad combination only · external / international N/A\n\n## Academic direction\n\nFlorida Warrington MSF: 32-credit UF undergrad combination only (not open externally). Deadlines Aug 30 / Oct 4 / Nov 11 within UF cycle. Tuition not published as flat MSF total. Related FinTech MS launches Fall 2027 for traditional applicants.\n\nOrientation: UF combo only · 32 credits · TFE #11 (2026) — external gap\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\nNot verified — Tuition not yet verified; 2026–27 per-credit schedule (program has no flat sticker).\n\nACCESS RESTRICTED (UF undergrad combination only; external/international N/A). CRITICAL ACCESS FLAG: William R. Hough MS in Finance is a combination/accelerated pathway — applications are only sought from current University of Florida undergraduates (apply in second year; min ~3.6 GPA). Not an open external Fall 2027 MSF for HK/TW/PRC applicants. 32 credits; 16 graduate credits may be taken before bachelor's finish; 12 credits double-count. Florida resident graduate rate $532.52/credit → 32× = $17,040.64. Combination + Bright Futures/Prepaid may further reduce cost for eligible FL students only. Missing program sticker ≠ 0.\n\nEstimate only: 32 graduate credits × $1,449.28 non-resident graduate rate (2026–27) = $46,376.96 — NOT a published MSF program sticker: $46,377. Per-credit graduate rates already include listed mandatory fee components (CITF, financial aid, technology, A&S, athletic, health, transportation). No separate MSF program fee schedule published. CRITICAL ACCESS FLAG: William R. Hough MS in Finance is a combination/accelerated pathway — applications are only sought from current University of Florida undergraduates (apply in second year; min ~3.6 GPA). Not an open external Fall 2027 MSF for HK/TW/PRC applicants. 32 credits; 16 graduate credits may be taken before bachelor's finish; 12 credits double-count. Florida resident graduate rate $532.52/credit → 32× = $17,040.64. Combination + Bright Futures/Prepaid may further reduce cost for eligible FL students only. Missing program sticker ≠ 0. Current UF undergraduates only per program admissions page.\n\nApplication timing: Early application · August 30 (year within UF sophomore cycle — not a standalone Fall 2027 external deadline). Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: not_required — MSF Program does not require a GMAT nor GRE score. SAT/ACT from UF undergrad record are electronically accessible; minimum expected SAT combined math+reading 1350/1600 or ACT math 31/36.\n- GMAT: optional — Applicants may submit a GMAT score to enhance the application; any GMAT received is included in comprehensive review. Program does not require GMAT.\n- TOEFL: not_required — Applications sought only from current UF undergraduates; English proficiency not listed on MSF page for this pathway.\n- IELTS: not_required — Same as TOEFL — UF undergrad combo pathway only.\n- English waiver: N/A for eligible UF undergraduates (program does not admit external/international applicants).\n- GPA: required — minimum 3.6 — scale 4.0 — Keep overall GPA above a 3.6; minimum 3.6 overall GPA expected for application. Average application GPA for MSF classes of 2026 and 2027 was 3.91.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two letters of recommendation emailed directly to Mrs. Hunt (Tayla.Hunt@warrington.ufl.edu) by recommenders.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Statement of purpose — Statement of purpose describing chosen career path and firms of interest; focus on junior summer internship targets with accompanying Excel/Word table of firms, caliber criteria, and recruitment process.\n- Resume: required — Resume formatted for finance industry; must include all post-high school education and employment and ongoing international affiliations/research funding per Florida Statute.\n- Transcripts: required — UF transcripts available electronically to MSF Admissions Committee from Student Information System; applicants do not need to order/email transcripts.\n- Interview: by_invitation — Candidates selected to interview should demonstrate characteristics appropriate for graduate business courses and qualifications expected by firms in their statement of purpose.\n- Fee: MSF program page does not state an application fee. Warrington specialized master's materials reference the UF Graduate School application; MBA section of masters-admissions page cites $30, but MSF combo page itself is silent.\n- Other: RESTRICTED: applications only sought from current UF undergraduates (combination bachelor's/master's).\n- Other: Pre-application form after first-year spring grades; full application in second year.\n- Other: SAT/ACT used from UF record (not GRE/GMAT).\n- Other: Complete required summer credits before third year; FIN/general business majors must complete 4000-level FIN prerequisites.\n\nExternal and international applicants are not eligible for classic florida-msf; see florida-msft (MS Finance and Technology) for an open path. Documented here for eligible UF undergrads only.\n\n- [MS Finance program / how to apply](https://warrington.ufl.edu/graduate/masters-finance/)\n- [Warrington Master's & MBA Admissions](https://warrington.ufl.edu/admissions-aid/masters-admissions/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: .\n\nShared scholarship IDs: No verified award links yet. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://warrington.ufl.edu/graduate/masters-finance/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://warrington.ufl.edu/admissions-aid/cost-aid/graduate/)\n- [MS Finance and Technology (related)](https://warrington.ufl.edu/graduate/masters-finance-technology/)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [UF 2026–27 Tuition and Fees (per credit)](https://cfo.ufl.edu/student-financial-resources/current-and-former-students/2026-27-academic-year-tuition-and-fees/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
