    "path": "05-finance/programs/illinois-msf.md",
    "title": "Illinois Gies — MSF",
    "body": "# Illinois Gies — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#19 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nIllinois Gies MSF: STEM, ~3 semesters / 40 cr. Fall 2027 rounds Oct 28’26–Jun 9’27 (intl final May 5). Est. intl tuition+fees $76,443 / resident $57,846 (2026–27 3-sem).\n\nOrientation: Fall or Spring · ~15 months / 40 cr · STEM · TFE #19 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$67,800 — Gies MSF international tuition total — 3 semesters × $22,600 (2026–27 estimates); 2026–27 estimates (table shows Fall '26 / Spring '27 / Fall '27 sequence for Fall 2026 cohort). Fall 2027 entrants: analogous 3-semester sequence; later-term rates may change — tuition guarantee locks entering-cohort rate once enrolled..\n\nMSF assessed per semester (not per credit), up to 20 credits/semester. US resident 3-semester total tuition+fees $57,846 (tuition $49,437 + fees $8,409). International total tuition+fees $76,443. Open external admits (not a UF/TAMU-style combination). Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nAlternate format: US resident tuition+campus fees estimate — 3 semesters (2026–27 rates) $57,846. Mandatory fees reference: $8,643. Campus fees international $2,881 × 3 semesters = $8,643 (2026–27 estimates on Gies MSF tuition page). Non-refundable deposit $1,750 credited to tuition after 10th day of first semester. MSF assessed per semester (not per credit), up to 20 credits/semester. US resident 3-semester total tuition+fees $57,846 (tuition $49,437 + fees $8,409). International total tuition+fees $76,443. Open external admits (not a UF/TAMU-style combination). Living cost band from official COA: $21,402–$29,705 (Registrar 2026–27 Grad additional expenses (intl): Food & Housing $16,512 + Books & Supplies $1,800 + Other $3,090 = $21,402 per academic year. Gies MSF domestic COA PDF lists Additional Expenses $9,935/semester (Food & Housing $7,490 + Books $900 + Other $1,545) → ×3 semesters = $29,705 (lifestyle-dependent).).\n\nApplication timing: Fall 2027 — Round 1 · 2026-10-28. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GMAT or GRE optional. Committee may request official scores if unable to decide from submitted materials. Institution code 1836. Upload unofficial score to portal while awaiting official.\n- GMAT: optional — Optional; same policy as GRE. Official to UIUC code 1836.\n- TOEFL: required — min 103 — Non-native speakers without Graduate College exemption: Full-status TOEFL iBT 103 (scores prior to 1/21/26) or 5.0 (scores after 1/20/26). Limited-status: 79 / 4.0. Official scores required; dated after Aug 1, 2025. Code 1836.\n- IELTS: required — min 7.5 — Full-status IELTS Academic 7.5; limited-status 6.5. Also Duolingo full 135 / limited 115.\n- English waiver: Graduate College English proficiency exemptions apply (see Grad College English Proficiency Requirements). Limited-status admits take English Placement Test on arrival; may require ESL coursework.\n- GPA: required — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — Illinois Graduate College minimum: GPA 3.0 (A=4.0) for last two years of undergraduate study. Programs may require higher; MSF page does not state a higher floor. Optional essay strongly recommended if GPA ≤3.0.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two references from academic and/or professional sources; signed and dated. Late LORs (>7 days after deadline) move application to next round.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Academic Statement of Purpose + personal statements — Academic Statement of Purpose 300–500 words total (background prep; how program helps goals; academic interests). Plus two short personal statements ≤250 words each.\n- Resume: required — Professional résumé ≤2 pages (education, work, internships, training, associations, leadership).\n- Transcripts: required — Most recent unofficial transcripts with name, institution, legend/scale. Diploma/certificate of degree if bachelor's earned. Official upon arrival if admitted. Check Grad College country requirements for U.S. bachelor's equivalence.\n- Interview: by_invitation — Required video essay component (3 randomly assigned questions, ~3 minutes). Live interview by invitation only if materials insufficient; decisions may be made with or without interview.\n- Fee: $90 — Non-refundable $90 for domestic and international. Cannot be processed without payment.\n- Other: Select program Finance → Finance - MS in Grad College portal.\n- Other: Optional essay available; scholarship acknowledgment in Financial Aid section for merit/need consideration.\n- Other: Passport/funding proof for internationals only after admission offer.\n\nFall 2027 Round 4 May 5, 2027 is final deadline for international applicants needing a new visa. Apply early for scholarship consideration.\n\n- [MSF Admissions](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/msf/admissions)\n- [Illinois Graduate College minimum requirements](https://grad.illinois.edu/admissions/graduate-admissions-minimum-requirements)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-110.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-110. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program hub / STEM](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/msf)\n- [Admissions / deadlines](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/msf/admissions)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/msf/tuition)\n- [Curriculum / credits](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/msf/curriculum)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [Gies MSF Estimated COA PDF (domestic 26–27)](https://giesbusiness.illinois.edu/docs/default-source/default-document-library/estimated-cost-of-attendance---gies-msf-domestic-26-27-(1).pdf?sfvrsn=787204dc_2)\n- [Illinois Registrar 26/27 Grad Additional Expenses](https://www.registrar.illinois.edu/tuition-fees/tuition-fee-rates/tf-rates-academic-year/g-additional-expenses-2627/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
