    "path": "05-finance/programs/msu-msf.md",
    "title": "Michigan State Broad — MSF",
    "body": "# Michigan State Broad — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#22 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Michigan State University\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nMSU Broad MS Finance: STEM (news), ~30 cr/~12 mo. Indexed deadlines Feb 1 / Mar 1 (years for 2027 entry). Indexed tuition 2026–27 $51k OOS / $46.5k in-state. VERIFY — Incapsula blocked live scrape.\n\nOrientation: Fall · ~12 months / 30 cr · STEM · TFE #22 (2026) — verify live\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$51,000 — Broad MSF out-of-state / international block tuition and departmental fees total (2026–27 AY); 2026–27 academic year (as stated on Broad MSF program page).\n\nSTEM; 30 credits; 12 months full-time on-campus only. Tuition page (broad.msu.edu/masters/finance/tuition/) was Incapsula-blocked to WebFetch/curl during research; dollar figures taken from live program overview page which publishes the same 2026–27 block amounts. 40% non-sponsored financial-support claim sourced from Wayback snapshot of the tuition page (archive 2026-05-18 still showed prior-year stickers $49,500/$45,000 but same 40% language). Open external admits. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nAlternate format: In-state program tuition 2026–27 (indexed tuition page) $46,500. Published $51,000 (OOS) / $46,500 (in-state) covers tuition charges for credits and departmental fees. Does not cover additional university fees, textbooks, course materials, or laptop (per tuition-page language mirrored on program overview and Wayback snapshot). Billed in three equal installments at start of each semester. STEM; 30 credits; 12 months full-time on-campus only. Tuition page (broad.msu.edu/masters/finance/tuition/) was Incapsula-blocked to WebFetch/curl during research; dollar figures taken from live program overview page which publishes the same 2026–27 block amounts. 40% non-sponsored financial-support claim sourced from Wayback snapshot of the tuition page (archive 2026-05-18 still showed prior-year stickers $49,500/$45,000 but same 40% language). Open external admits.\n\nApplication timing: Round 1 · 2027-02-01 · Month/day from indexed Broad admissions page; year assigned for Fall 2027 entry — verify on live page. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — min 310 — GRE minimum 310 verbal+quantitative combined, or GMAT. Scores <5 years old. Waiver may be requested at application; current MSU undergrads in good academic standing eligible to waive.\n- GMAT: required — min 600 — GMAT minimum 600 (code QH0-5P-69) or GRE. Waiver may be requested; current MSU undergrads in good standing eligible to waive.\n- TOEFL: required — min 100 — International: TOEFL iBT minimum 100 (paper 600 / computer 250). School code 1465, dept 4102. Lower/no scores may allow provisional admission per university rules.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS band minimum 7.\n- English waiver: Not detailed beyond provisional admission language for lower/missing scores; confirm with program.\n- GPA: required — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — Four-year undergrad degree with cumulative GPA 3.0 or higher expected.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two letters required; at least one desirably from a faculty member (course or research). Address listed on admissions page for mailed letters.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Statement of objectives — Statement of objectives included in overall record review (cited under Admission Criteria).\n- Resume: not_stated — Resume/CV not listed in Application Requirements checklist on MS Finance admissions page (work experience is an admission criterion).\n- Transcripts: required — Scanned transcripts and degree certificates in online application; original/certified required if recommended for admission.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not mentioned on MS Finance admissions page.\n- Fee: $50 — $50 due at application submission.\n- Other: At least two years full-time post-bachelor work experience normally expected; waivable for exceptional candidates.\n- Other: Prerequisites: equivalents of MTH 124 Survey of Calculus I and STT 315 Intro Probability and Statistics for Business.\n- Other: Major code 6016, Major: Finance.\n- Other: Working knowledge of Internet, word processing, spreadsheets.\n\nIncapsula often blocks automated fetches of broad.msu.edu — verify live page before applying. Request GMAT/GRE waiver only if clearly eligible.\n\n- [Admissions (official)](https://broad.msu.edu/masters/finance/admissions/)\n- [Program hub](https://broad.msu.edu/masters/finance/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-113.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-113. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://broad.msu.edu/masters/finance/)\n- [Admissions (indexed)](https://broad.msu.edu/masters/finance/admissions/)\n- [Tuition (indexed)](https://broad.msu.edu/masters/finance/tuition/)\n- [STEM designation news](https://broad.msu.edu/news/two-broad-masters-programs-earn-stem-designation/)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [Wayback Broad MSF Tuition page](https://web.archive.org/web/20260518190554/https://broad.msu.edu/masters/finance/tuition/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
