    "path": "05-finance/programs/notredame-msf.md",
    "title": "Notre Dame Mendoza — MSF",
    "body": "# Notre Dame Mendoza — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#15 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of Notre Dame\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nNotre Dame Mendoza MSF: STEM; June summer start; 38 credits / ~11 months. Tuition 2026–27 $74,618. Rounds Sep 10 EA / Oct 20 / Jan 7 (intl) / Mar 17.\n\nOrientation: Summer (June) start · ~11 months · STEM · TFE #15 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$74,618 — MSF tuition for 2026–2027 academic year (Summer + Fall/Spring); 2026–27.\n\nSUMMER START. STEM. Start Date June (summer). 38 credit hours. Tuition split on COA: Summer $21,604 + Fall/Spring $53,014 = $74,618. Total program COA published $111,298 including living. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nMandatory fees reference: $2,600. Financial Aid COA: Summer fees $400 + Fall/Spring fees $2,200 (= program fee $1,600 + student fees $600 on Mendoza breakdown) = $2,600. Mendoza page also lists Program Fee $1,600 (Fall/Spring) and Student Fees $400 summer / $600 Fall/Spring. STEM. Start Date June (summer). 38 credit hours. Tuition split on COA: Summer $21,604 + Fall/Spring $53,014 = $74,618. Total program COA published $111,298 including living. Living cost band from official COA: $21,285 (ND Financial Aid MSF COA housing and food: Summer $3,465 + Fall/Spring $17,820 = $21,285. Books/supplies $400+$1,750; personal $700+$6,720; transportation $525+$2,700 also published.). SUMMER START — matriculation is not a standard autumn-only Fall intake.\n\nApplication timing: Early Action · 2026-09-10. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GMAT or GRE not required if applicant has or will have undergraduate degree from a U.S. college/university prior to enrollment. Applicants from colleges/universities outside the U.S. must submit valid GMAT or apply for GMAT waiver. Scores ≤5 years. GRE code 6998.\n- GMAT: optional — Not required for U.S. bachelor's holders/expected graduates. Required for non-U.S. institution applicants unless waiver granted via waiver form. GMAT code XM7-2D-68.\n- TOEFL: required — Non-U.S. citizen applicants (and U.S. citizens with extensive international study) must submit English proficiency. Mendoza MSF page accepts TOEFL; does not publish a minimum score. Mendoza TOEFL code 2456. ND Graduate School publishes TOEFL iBT 80 (pre-Feb 2026; Speaking ≥23) or 4.5 avg / no section <4.0 (updated) — cite Grad School separately; confirm with Mendoza if program-specific floor differs.\n- IELTS: required — IELTS accepted on Mendoza MSF page; minimum not published there. ND Graduate School lists IELTS 7.0 composite.\n- English waiver: May be waived if completed at least six full-time semesters or nine full-time quarters at a university where English is the primary language (transcripts verify; committee may request more).\n- GPA: not_stated — No minimum GPA stated on MSF apply page.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 1 — One recommendation; someone familiar with professional or academic background who can offer detailed assessment.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Written statement — Written statement ≤500 words: detailed post-master's career plans; how background + Notre Dame studies equip you; short- and long-term goals with industry and function.\n- Resume: required — One-page resume summarizing education, work experience, skills, accomplishments.\n- Transcripts: required — From all colleges/universities attended including summer and graduate study. International transcripts need official English translation. Unofficial OK for application; official final with proof of graduation before enrollment if admitted. Degree audits not accepted.\n- Interview: required — Video assessment required after application submission (Admissions Committee questions); must complete to move forward. Not framed as optional invitation-only live interview.\n- Fee: $50 — waivers: U.S. Active Duty Military or Veterans; current/former Peace Corps; current/former Teach for America — contact msf.business@nd.edu. — $50 non-refundable; pay via application status page after submit. Application incomplete until paid.\n- Other: Applicant Snapshot: required 4-slide PDF deck (no audio/video).\n- Other: Optional supplemental essay for additional context.\n- Other: Also accepts PTE Academic and Duolingo for English (mins not on Mendoza MSF page).\n\nInternational applicants strongly encouraged to apply by Round 2 for visa timing. Non-U.S. undergrad degree holders: plan GMAT or GMAT waiver early.\n\n- [MSF Application](https://mendoza.nd.edu/graduate-programs/finance-msf/apply/)\n- [MSF program hub](https://mendoza.nd.edu/graduate-programs/finance-msf/)\n- [ND Graduate School international English (mins reference)](https://graduateschool.nd.edu/admissions/international-students/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-103.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-103. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program hub](https://mendoza.nd.edu/graduate-programs/finance-msf/)\n- [Apply / deadlines](https://mendoza.nd.edu/graduate-programs/finance-msf/apply/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://mendoza.nd.edu/graduate-programs/finance-msf/tuition-financial-aid/)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [ND Financial Aid Finance (MSF) costs](https://financialaid.nd.edu/apply-or-renew/graduate-students/graduate-program-costs/finance-msf/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
