    "path": "05-finance/programs/nyu-courant-mf.md",
    "title": "NYU Courant Institute — MSF",
    "body": "# NYU Courant Institute — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#11 in QuantNet 2026 Ranking of Best Financial Engineering Programs (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nSeparate quant-mfe track. Not a TFE Times MSF rank. tfeRank2026 is null on every row. Stanford ICME MCF is not on the 2026 QuantNet list (QuantNet rank null).\n\nRanking provenance: [IBKR Quant News](https://www.interactivebrokers.com/campus/ibkr-quant-news/2026-quantnet-ranking-of-best-financial-engineering-programs/).\n\nUniversity: New York University\n\nDegree route: MS in Mathematics in Finance\n\nApplication status: Fall 2027 (full-time Fall-only); part-time Fall or Spring\n\n## Academic direction\n\nNYU Courant Math Finance: FT deadline Feb 12 (2027 cycle — verify year). 36 points / 3 sem. GSAS ~$2,426/cr. STEM CIP 27.0305. QuantNet #11.\n\nOrientation: Fall FT · 3 semesters · QuantNet #11 · SEPARATE TRACK\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$87,336 — Estimated tuition 36 points × GSAS $2,426/credit (2026–27 NYU Bursar); 2026–27 GSAS rate × 36 points.\n\nSEPARATE TRACK quant-mfe. id=nyu-courant-mf (NOT nyu-courant). FT Fall-only; summer internship between sem 2–3; optional August bootcamp. STEM. Program states it does not accept applications for financial assistance. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nMandatory fees reference: $4,425. GSAS Registration & Services Fee $503/semester + $81 per credit. Illustrative 3-semester FT path: 3×$503 + 36×$81 = $1,509 + $2,916 = $4,425 (assumes all 36 points billed under GSAS R&S schedule). Confirm actual semester credit splits with program. SEPARATE TRACK quant-mfe. id=nyu-courant-mf (NOT nyu-courant). FT Fall-only; summer internship between sem 2–3; optional August bootcamp. STEM. Program states it does not accept applications for financial assistance. NYU Bursar 2026–27: Graduate School of Arts and Science All Programs $2,426 per credit + $503 registration/services fee + $81 per-credit R&S fee. 36-point degree → tuition $87,336 before fees. Program points to NYU tuition calculator. Living cost band not published for this program (null, not zero).\n\nApplication timing: Full-time Fall (all materials to GSAS) · 2027-02-12 · Program page lists February 12 without year; assigned to Fall 2027 cycle — re-confirm on GSAS for 2027. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — Official general GRE required for M.S. (FT and PT). Subject GRE in math/physics/other quant encouraged. Highly quantitative PhD holders may email cims-mathfin-app@nyu.edu with transcript to request GRE waiver. GSAS code 2596. Most accepted students >90th percentile quant (descriptive).\n- GMAT: not_accepted — GMAT not accepted for standard M.S. (Courant admissions page). Dual MathFin/MBA may use GMAT or GRE for GSAS; GMAT otherwise not a substitute for GRE per GSAS test-scores page.\n- TOEFL: required — min 100 — TOEFL/IELTS/Duolingo required unless native English, U.S. citizen/PR, or baccalaureate/master’s at English-instruction institution. GSAS recommends TOEFL ≥100 (legacy) / ≥5 (new scale from Jan 2026), DET ≥130, IELTS ≥7; lower scores may still apply. Code 2596; TOEFL Essentials/ITP not accepted.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS accepted; GSAS recommends overall band ≥7.\n- English waiver: Native English speaker; OR U.S. citizen/PR; OR completed/will complete baccalaureate or master’s where language of instruction is English (supporting letter if transcript unclear).\n- GPA: not_stated — No required minimum GPA (Courant admissions FAQ).\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 3 — Three LORs; ≥2 from instructors of advanced math/quant/CS/engineering. FT: ≥1 math-focused and ≥1 CS/programming-focused preferred. Manager letter OK if significant work experience.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as statement of purpose / statement of academic purpose — Three topics ≤150 words each (career motivation; interesting math/science fact; research/class/internship). Optional separate Personal Statement for extra info.\n- Resume: required — Professional CV/resume with education, employment (company/division/dates/location/responsibilities), non-academic activities.\n- Transcripts: required — One official academic transcript from each post-secondary institution (upload in online application); official scores/transcripts needed to complete review.\n- Interview: required — Full-time applicants must submit a short video statement (≤5 minutes) addressing a challenging experience/project relevance to quant finance OR a preferred quant-finance area and fit. Not a live interview; required application video.\n- Fee: $150 — waivers: Not stated on Courant admissions page. — Non-refundable $150 (Courant admissions FAQ).\n- Other: FT Fall-only (deadline Feb 12); PT Aug 1 Fall / Dec 1 Spring.\n- Other: After submit: no updated grades/resumes/experience accepted.\n- Other: Apply to only one Courant Math Finance program at a time.\n\nGRE required (GMAT not accepted for standard MS). Required video statement for FT/PT MS.\n\n- [Courant Math Finance admissions](https://math-finance.cims.nyu.edu/admissions/)\n- [GSAS Mathematics in Finance requirements](https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/arc/programs/mathematics-in-finance.html)\n- [GSAS Test Scores](https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/arc/test-scores.html)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nNYU Courant Mathematics in Finance does not accept applications for program financial assistance (as of 2026-10-26). No program scholarship card is ingested.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: No verified award links yet. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Admissions / deadlines](https://math-finance.cims.nyu.edu/admissions/)\n- [Academics / 36 points](https://math-finance.cims.nyu.edu/academics/)\n- [NYU Bulletin Mathematics in Finance MS](https://bulletins.nyu.edu/graduate/arts-science/programs/mathematics-finance-ms/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.nyu.edu/content/dam/nyu/bursar/documents/2026-2027%20Tuition%20and%20Fees.pdf)\n- [QuantNet 2026 MFE ranking via IBKR Quant News](https://www.interactivebrokers.com/campus/ibkr-quant-news/2026-quantnet-ranking-of-best-financial-engineering-programs/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
