    "body": "# Ohio State Fisher — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#21 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: The Ohio State University\n\nDegree route: Specialized Master in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nOSU Fisher SMF: STEM, 36 cr/~16 mo, Autumn only (Aug 24 2027). Deadlines Dec 11’26 / Feb 19 / May 28 intl / Jul 19 dom. Est. NR/intl $68,093 / OH $47,093 (2026–27).\n\nOrientation: Autumn (Aug) · ~16 months · STEM · TFE #21 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$68,093 — Fisher SMF non-resident and international estimated tuition and fees — 36 credit hours / 3 semesters (2026–27); 2026–27 academic year estimates (subject to change for future terms).\n\nSpecialized Master in Finance (SMF); STEM; 16 months / 3 semesters; Autumn entry only (Autumn 2027 classes begin Aug 24, 2027). Ohio resident tuition and fees $47,093. Forever Buckeye / residency pathways may change classification for some students — not assumed for intl.\n\nAlternate format: Ohio resident tuition+fees estimate — 36 credits / 3 semesters (2026–27) $47,093. Published $68,093 already includes General Fee, Tuition & Instruction Fee, Student Activity Fee, Student Union Fee, Recreation Fee, Learning-Technology Fee, COTA Bus Fee. Student Health Insurance $4,108 (9 months) separate; international students cannot waive. Specialized Master in Finance (SMF); STEM; 16 months / 3 semesters; Autumn entry only (Autumn 2027 classes begin Aug 24, 2027). Ohio resident tuition and fees $47,093. Forever Buckeye / residency pathways may change classification for some students — not assumed for intl. Living cost band from official COA: $21,502 (Fisher SMF page Estimated Other Expenses (9 months): Housing, food & misc. $19,986 + Books and Supplies $1,516 = $21,502 (excludes Student Health Insurance $4,108). Program spans 16 months — summer/living beyond 9 months not itemized on page.).\n\nApplication timing: Priority 1 (merit aid) · 2026-12-11. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GMAT or GRE optional (no preference). Scores valid 5 years. From Oct 1, 2024 only GRE taken at an ETS testing center accepted (not at-home); valid at-home GRE before that date still accepted. Apply without scores by answering YES to the no-score question.\n- GMAT: optional — GMAT or GRE optional (no preference). Scores valid 5 years. Holistic review; test scores may strengthen application if submitted.\n- TOEFL: required — min 79 — TOEFL iBT or Home Edition minimum 79 (4.0 on updated TOEFL launched Jan 2026). MyBest not accepted. Official scores ≤2 years old. ETS code 1592.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS Academic or Online minimum 7.0. One Skill Retake not accepted. Fisher international page lists 7.0 (university GPAdmissions general page lists 6.5).\n- English waiver: Exempt if citizen of, or bachelor’s+ from, listed English-speaking countries/territories (Fisher international applicants page / gpadmissions.osu.edu). Duolingo also accepted (min 120). Degree from U.S. university also commonly cited for TOEFL waiver in Fisher FAQs.\n- GPA: not_stated — No numeric minimum GPA stated on SMF applying page. Four-year bachelor’s (or equivalent) required; OSU generally does not treat 3-year bachelor’s as equivalent.\n- Letters of recommendation: optional — Two references required (Admissions may contact). Formal letters of recommendation are optional; if supplied, recommenders email to FCOB-grad_apps@osu.edu with application ID. Apps may be reviewed before optional letters arrive.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Essay — Required essay: short- and long-term goals and how/why SMF helps achieve them. Recommended max 750 words. Optional supplemental essay (max ~500 words).\n- Resume: required — Resume required; may exceed one page covering employment, extracurriculars, languages, military if applicable.\n- Transcripts: required — Official transcripts from each undergrad/grad institution where credit earned (scanned official for review; verified electronic to GPADOCS@osu.edu or mailed). International: original language + certified English translation.\n- Interview: required — Required Kira online recorded video interview for every applicant; application not reviewed until complete. Live interviews on a need-basis only.\n- Fee: $60 — waivers: International applicants pay $70. — Nonrefundable $60 USD domestic (U.S. citizens/permanent residents/asylees); $70 international. Paid by credit card with online application.\n- Other: No prerequisite courses; no post-undergrad work experience required (~75% of admits have <1 year).\n- Other: Quantitative aptitude valued via coursework or GMAT/GRE.\n- Other: AI policy: original voice required; limited AI for proofreading/brainstorming with disclosure; AI-generated content may disqualify.\n- Other: Autumn 2027 application open; rolling review; priority/final deadlines posted on applying page.\n\nComplete Kira video early; optional GMAT/GRE can help if quant background is thin. Apply early for merit aid (Priority 1 Dec 11, 2026).\n\n- [Applying & deadlines](https://fisher.osu.edu/graduate/smf/admissions/applying-fisher)\n- [International applicants / English minima](https://fisher.osu.edu/graduate/international-applicants)\n- [Program hub](https://fisher.osu.edu/graduate/smf)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-111, SCH-112.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-111, SCH-112. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program hub / STEM](https://fisher.osu.edu/graduate/smf)\n- [Applying & deadlines](https://fisher.osu.edu/graduate/smf/admissions/applying-fisher)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://fisher.osu.edu/graduate/smf/admissions/tuition-funding)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
