    "title": "RIT Saunders — MSF",
    "body": "# RIT Saunders — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#29 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Rochester Institute of Technology\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nRIT Saunders Finance MS: STEM-OPT FT, Fall/Spring rolling. Tuition per RIT grad schedule (null flat). Credits not on program page (null). Flexible FinTech-heavy curriculum.\n\nOrientation: Fall/Spring rolling · STEM-OPT (FT) · TFE #29 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\nNot verified — Tuition not yet verified; 2026–27 graduate tuition.\n\nRIT graduate billing 2026–27: $2,690/credit if <12 credits/sem OR fixed $32,271/sem for 12–18 credits. Finance MS total credit hours NOT stated on rit.edu/study/finance-ms this pass (secondary sources cite 31 — left null). On-campus only; Fall or Spring; STEM-OPT eligible for full-time. Open external admits. Use RIT estimate tool once plan of study / credits confirmed. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nNo flat program sticker. Graduate billing: $2,690/credit when under 12 credits per semester, or $32,271 per semester for 12–18 credits. Total depends on credit pacing; Finance MS credit hours are not stated on the program page. When FT (9+ credits/sem): Student Activity Fee $235/sem + Student Health Services Fee $315/sem. International students automatically enrolled/billed for RIT health insurance (amount not on estimate page this pass). No Finance MS flat total published. RIT graduate billing 2026–27: $2,690/credit if <12 credits/sem OR fixed $32,271/sem for 12–18 credits. Finance MS total credit hours NOT stated on rit.edu/study/finance-ms this pass (secondary sources cite 31 — left null). On-campus only; Fall or Spring; STEM-OPT eligible for full-time. Open external admits. Use RIT estimate tool once plan of study / credits confirmed. Living cost band from official COA: $20,386 (RIT Estimate Graduate Education Costs page (linked from Finance MS): estimated living expenses (housing and meals) $17,370/year + estimated transportation, books, supplies, and personal expenses $3,016/year = $20,386. General graduate estimate — not a Finance-MS-only COA table.).\n\nApplication timing: Fall / Spring — Rolling · Program page: Application Deadline = Rolling for full-time and part-time. Apply early for visa timing; no fixed final date published on program page.. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GRE or GMAT optional, but recommended for individuals with degrees from international universities.\n- GMAT: optional — GRE or GMAT optional; recommended for international-university degree holders.\n- TOEFL: required — min 88 — Program table: TOEFL 88 / 4.5 (new scale). Also DET 130, LanguageCert Academic 74, PTE Academic 60. Some internationals may get English test waiver per RIT policy. Conditional admission possible below minimum.\n- IELTS: required — min 6.5 — IELTS 6.5. Balanced subscores expected.\n- English waiver: May be considered if worked/studied in U.S. last two years; bachelor’s/master’s from English-medium university in RIT waiver territory list; or citizen of listed territories with English-medium secondary school. See RIT graduate apply page.\n- GPA: recommended — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — Baccalaureate from accredited university; minimum cumulative GPA 3.0 (or equivalent) recommended.\n- Letters of recommendation: optional — Letters of recommendation are optional for Finance MS. (RIT College of Business master’s generally excepted from required LOR rule on university apply page.)\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Personal statement of educational objectives — Personal statement of educational objectives required (open-ended; may address why program, career goals, non-academic qualities, prior experience, why RIT).\n- Resume: required — Current resume or curriculum vitae required.\n- Transcripts: required — Copies of official transcripts (English) of all prior undergrad/grad coursework including transfer credit.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not listed on Finance MS admissions details.\n- Fee: $65 — waivers: Current RIT students and RIT alumni not required to pay; fee waived within 24 hours of submission for them. Other waiver categories per Grad FAQ. — Non-refundable $65 graduate application fee (RIT Graduate How to Apply).\n- Other: STEM-OPT eligible; on-campus only.\n- Other: Fall priority Jan 15 / standard Mar 1; Spring rolling.\n- Other: International F-1 must study full-time.\n\nInternational-degree applicants should strongly consider submitting GRE/GMAT despite optional status.\n\n- [Finance MS admissions](https://www.rit.edu/study/finance-ms)\n- [Graduate how to apply / fee / English](https://www.rit.edu/admissions/graduate/apply)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-123.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-123. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program hub / STEM-OPT / rolling](https://www.rit.edu/study/finance-ms)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.rit.edu/admissions/graduate/estimate-education-costs)\n- [Graduate admission deadlines overview](https://www.rit.edu/admissions/graduate-admission-deadlines-and-requirements)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [Graduate Funding Sources](https://www.rit.edu/admissions/financial-aid/graduate-funding-sources)\n- [RIT Tuition and Fees (grad table)](https://www.rit.edu/admissions/tuition-and-fees)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
