    "path": "05-finance/programs/rochester-msf.md",
    "title": "Rochester Simon — MSF",
    "body": "# Rochester Simon — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#10 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of Rochester\n\nDegree route: Full-Time MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nRochester Simon MS in Finance (STEM): Fall start; 9-mo or 16-mo internship track. Tuition 2026–27 $78,000/year (+$5,500 internship option). Fall rounds Oct 15 / Jan 5 / Mar 1 / May 1 (years for 2027 entry).\n\nOrientation: Fall · 9 or 16 months · STEM · TFE #10 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$78,000 — Full-Time MS in Finance tuition per year (2026–27 AY); 2026–27 (rates accurate as of 2025-11-14 per Simon page).\n\nSTEM. Tracks: 9-month non-internship vs 16-month internship (+$5,500 fee). Tuition published as $/year — 9-mo track typically one billed year; 16-mo may extend across a second academic year (second-year tuition not separately itemized on page — missing ≠ 0 for multi-year total). Fall entry for MS Finance per admissions FAQs (curriculum page spring banner appears shared/MS-wide — treat Fall as SoT for Finance). Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nMandatory fees reference: $1,827. Activity Fee $800/year + Mandatory Health Fee $1,027/year (health fees are estimates pending NY State approval in June). Health Insurance $3,906/year separate. Intl: ISO Fee $140/year + International Student Programming Fee $900 one-time. Optional Internship Track fee $5,500. STEM. Tracks: 9-month non-internship vs 16-month internship (+$5,500 fee). Tuition published as $/year — 9-mo track typically one billed year; 16-mo may extend across a second academic year (second-year tuition not separately itemized on page — missing ≠ 0 for multi-year total). Fall entry for MS Finance per admissions FAQs (curriculum page spring banner appears shared/MS-wide — treat Fall as SoT for Finance). Living cost band from official COA: $22,505 (Simon published 2026–27 MSF living: Housing $10,206 + Food $6,273 + Travel $2,250 + Personal $2,466 + Books $1,310 = $22,505/year (excludes health insurance).).\n\nApplication timing: Round 1 · 2026-10-15 · 11:59 p.m. ET. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — Option to apply without GMAT/GRE. Encouraged to review standardized test guidance / class profile middle 80% if deciding whether to submit. GRE code 2972.\n- GMAT: optional — Optional. Full-Time MS in Finance GMAT code WX9-8R-36. Single test-date scores; Superscore considered only as additional data.\n- TOEFL: required — Required for intl whose native language is not English (TOEFL iBT / Home / Essentials). Preferred minimum referenced on admissions page but numeric value not clearly extractable from page text this pass. Code 7260.\n- IELTS: required — IELTS (incl. Indicator) accepted. Preferred minimum referenced but numeric not clearly extractable from admissions page text.\n- English waiver: Waived if attended ≥3 academic years post-secondary taught solely in English AND received bachelor’s or master’s from English-instruction college/university. Upload supporting waiver documentation. Duolingo also accepted. Proof of English proficiency required for visa issuance.\n- GPA: not_stated — No hard minimum GPA on admissions checklist; scholarship guidance example mentions 3.2+ as one factor among many.\n- Letters of recommendation: not_stated — Official FAQ: Simon does not accept letters of recommendation.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Required essay — One required essay for MS (word count on checklist 400–700; 2026 sneak-peek blog lists 250–500 for goals/backup/fit prompts—confirm live application). Video essay is MBA-only / not in MS application per 2026 requirements blog.\n- Resume: required — Business-formatted résumé (not CV), recommend ≤2 pages; quantify accomplishments.\n- Transcripts: required — School-issued transcripts scanned/uploaded for each college; undergrad and graduate if applicable. English or certified translation. Proof of degree conferral.\n- Interview: not_used — Per 2026 application-requirements blog, optional video essay is for MBA candidates only and not included in MS application. FAQ/checklist do not list a live MS interview.\n- Fee: $90 — waivers: Active-duty military/veterans; University of Rochester alumni; official US community/country service (e.g., TFA, Peace Corps); live webinar/event attendees. Request ≥5 business days before deadline and before submit. — Non-refundable $90 USD by credit card in application.\n- Other: Fall entry only for MS Finance\n- Other: No official academic prerequisites for MS Finance\n- Other: 3-year bachelor’s accepted\n- Other: Merit scholarships automatic with application review (>90% of incoming MS get merit aid per site)\n\nIntl: English test or documented waiver; scores needed for visa. No LORs accepted—strengthen essay/resume/quant profile. Apply early rounds for faster decision and scholarship pools.\n\n- [Full-Time MS Admissions](https://simon.rochester.edu/programs/full-time-ms/admissions)\n- [Admissions FAQs](https://simon.rochester.edu/programs/full-time-ms/admissions/admissions-faqs)\n- [Fee waiver](https://simon.rochester.edu/programs/full-time-ms/admissions/admissions-faqs/fee-waiver)\n- [Standardized tests](https://simon.rochester.edu/programs/full-time-ms/admissions/admissions-faqs/standardized-tests)\n- [2026 application requirements blog](https://simon.rochester.edu/blog/admissions-blog/sneak-peek-2026-full-time-application-requirements)\n- [MS Finance hub](https://simon.rochester.edu/programs/full-time-ms-in-finance)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-097, SCH-098.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-097, SCH-098. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Program hub](https://simon.rochester.edu/programs/full-time-ms-in-finance)\n- [Curriculum / tracks](https://simon.rochester.edu/programs/full-time-ms-in-finance/curriculum)\n- [Admissions / Fall deadlines](https://simon.rochester.edu/programs/full-time-ms/admissions)\n- [Full-Time MS deadlines (alt calendar)](https://simon.rochester.edu/full-time-ms-deadlines)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://simon.rochester.edu/programs/full-time-ms/tuition-financial-aid)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
