    "body": "# Texas A&M Mays — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#20 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Texas A&M University\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance (TAMU 4+1)\n\nApplication status: TAMU undergrad 4+1 only · external / international N/A\n\n## Academic direction\n\nTAMU Mays MSF: TAMU-undergrad 4+1 only; May boot camps then FT year; 36 cr. Tuition via calculator (null flat). External Fall 2027 gap — related MS-QFIN may accept non-TAMU grads (verify deadlines).\n\nOrientation: TAMU combo + May boot camps · 36 cr · TFE #20 (2026) — external gap\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\nNot verified — Tuition not yet verified; 2026–27 · No open external Fall 2027 sticker.\n\nSUMMER START. ACCESS RESTRICTED (TAMU undergrad 4+1 only; external/international N/A). CRITICAL ACCESS FLAG: Mays MS Finance is a 4+1 / combination pathway. Official page and catalog: All applicants must currently be enrolled as undergraduates at Texas A&M University (sophomore-start and senior-start tracks). Not an open external Fall 2027 MSF for HK/TW/PRC applicants. 36 credit hours, College Station in-person. External applicants seeking finance master's are pointed by Mays marketing to other programs (e.g., Master of Financial Management) — out of this MSF id scope.\n\nNo flat MSF program sticker published for external admits. ISSS 2025 one Fall-or-Spring estimate lists MS Finance student total $38,188 including tuition/fees/insurance and living for one major term only — not a full-degree sticker; not used as Fall 2027 program total (missing ≠ invent multi-term sum). CRITICAL ACCESS FLAG: Mays MS Finance is a 4+1 / combination pathway. Official page and catalog: All applicants must currently be enrolled as undergraduates at Texas A&M University (sophomore-start and senior-start tracks). Not an open external Fall 2027 MSF for HK/TW/PRC applicants. 36 credit hours, College Station in-person. External applicants seeking finance master's are pointed by Mays marketing to other programs (e.g., Master of Financial Management) — out of this MSF id scope. May mini-mester boot camps follow admission for the TAMU 4+1 pathway (summer structure; not an open external autumn matriculation). Do not merge with tamu-qfin / MS Quantitative Finance. Current Texas A&M undergraduates only (sophomores/seniors) per Mays 4+1 MS Finance and TAMU catalog. SUMMER START — matriculation is not a standard autumn-only Fall intake.\n\nApplication timing: 2027–28 cycle opens · 2027-04-01 · TAMU undergrad 4+1 only (external / international N/A) · Rising sophomores / seniors only. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — Minimum 50th percentile on quantitative portion. Waived for those with GPA of 3.5 or higher in STEM, Business, or ECON majors. Program details: Sophomore Start also notes minimum 50th percentile GRE Q with minimum GPA 3.0 emphasis.\n- GMAT: unknown — GMAT not mentioned on 4+1 MS Finance hub or program-details pages; GRE is the listed standardized test.\n- TOEFL: not_required — Program restricted to current Texas A&M undergraduates; English proficiency exams not listed among admission requirements.\n- IELTS: not_required — Same — TAMU undergrad 4+1 pathway only.\n- English waiver: N/A for eligible TAMU undergraduates (external/international N/A).\n- GPA: required — minimum 3.25 — scale 4.0 — Minimum GPA 3.25 overall; 3.5 for FINC majors (hub). Program-details Sophomore Start text also cites minimum GPA 3.0 with GRE Q ≥50th percentile — hub list is the primary published requirement set.\n- Letters of recommendation: not_stated — LOR not listed among published admission requirements on hub or program-details pages.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Essay — Essay required (listed on admission requirements).\n- Resume: required — Resume required.\n- Transcripts: required — Unofficial transcript required at application.\n- Interview: by_invitation — Program-details: Apply through April 15 to be interviewed in the spring semester. Not stated whether every applicant is interviewed.\n- Fee: Application fee not stated on 4+1 MS Finance hub or program-details pages.\n- Other: RESTRICTED: all applicants must currently be enrolled as undergraduates at Texas A&M University (College Station).\n- Other: Attend information session (listed requirement).\n- Other: Prerequisites (B or better) due after admission by end of spring following application: ACCT 209/229/640 and ECON 202 or 203.\n- Other: Sophomore Start and Senior Start pathways; few spots for seniors (senior start needs ≥1 commercial internship).\n\nExternal and international applicants are not eligible for classic tamu-msf 4+1; see tamu-qfin for a separate open quantitative path. Pages currently emphasize Fall 2026 entry cycles; 2027–28 cycle opens Apr 1, 2027.\n\n- [4+1 MS Finance hub](https://mays.tamu.edu/graduate/masters/4plus1/ms-finance/)\n- [Program details](https://mays.tamu.edu/graduate/masters/4plus1/ms-finance/program-details/)\n- [TAMU catalog MS Finance](https://catalog.tamu.edu/graduate/colleges-schools-interdisciplinary/business/finance/ms/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nNo verified program-tied scholarship for tamu-msf — Aggie 4+1 only, not open to external Fall 2027 admits (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nShared scholarship IDs: No verified award links yet. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://mays.tamu.edu/graduate/masters/4plus1/ms-finance/)\n- [Program details / May boot camps](https://mays.tamu.edu/graduate/masters/4plus1/ms-finance/program-details/)\n- [MS Quantitative Finance catalog (related)](https://catalog.tamu.edu/graduate/colleges-schools-interdisciplinary/business/finance/quantitative-finance-ms/)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [TAMU Catalog MS in Finance](https://catalog.tamu.edu/graduate/colleges-schools-interdisciplinary/business/finance/ms/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
