    "title": "UC Irvine Merage — MSF",
    "body": "# UC Irvine Merage — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#13 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of California, Irvine\n\nDegree route: Master of Finance (MFin)\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUCI Merage MFin: STEM, 12 months, 52 units. Rounds Oct 15 / Dec 1 / Feb 1 / Apr 1 / May 15 / Jul 15 (years for Fall 2027). Program fee Fall 2026 cohort $80,848 (Fall 2027 TBD).\n\nOrientation: Fall · 12 months · STEM · TFE #13 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$80,848 — Master of Finance program fee total — cohort entering Fall 2026 (4 quarters × $20,212); 2026–27 schedule for Fall 2026 entering cohort (posted 2026-08-14). Fall 2027 entering cohort rates NOT separately published as of asOf — do not treat as locked Fall 2027 quote..\n\nSTEM. 12-month / 4-quarter full-time MFin (52 units). Merage financial-aid page points to Registrar fee assessment; living budget published for nine months (F/W/S) only — summer living not in that table. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nMandatory fees reference: $9,985. Mandatory campus fees on Fall 2026 cohort schedule (excl. optional UCGPC ~$7): Student Services Access $1,096 + Assoc. Grad Students $56 + Student Center $617.27 + Bren Events $92 + Recreation $352 + Student Health Insurance $7,771.86 ≈ $9,985.13. Total fees paid on schedule $90,833.13 including program fee. STEM. 12-month / 4-quarter full-time MFin (52 units). Merage financial-aid page points to Registrar fee assessment; living budget published for nine months (F/W/S) only — summer living not in that table. Living cost band from official COA: $21,992–$38,640 (Merage MFin nine-month budget (Fall/Winter/Spring): Books $2,009 + Personal $3,489 + Transportation $3,663 + Room & Board Living at Home $12,831 (= $21,992) to Off-Campus Apartments $29,479 (= $38,640). On-campus Palo Verde R&B $17,222 mid. Does not include Summer quarter.).\n\nApplication timing: Round 1 · 2026-10-15. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GMAT or GRE is not required. Optional; strongly recommended if GPA under 3.0 per FAQs. Scores valid up to five years. GRE code 4859.\n- GMAT: optional — Not required; optional additional data point. GMAT code 0DP-7R-40.\n- TOEFL: required — min 80 — International students if applicable. Minimum TOEFL iBT 80/120 or 4.0/6.0 (new scale). Valid up to two years. Institution code 4859.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS Academic minimum overall 7, with no individual module less than 6. Electronic scores only from test center.\n- English waiver: Waived if undergraduate or graduate degree from a U.S. institution or institution where English was the sole language of instruction per World Higher Education Database (WHED).\n- GPA: not_stated — No minimum GPA published on admissions page. FAQs recommend GMAT/GRE if GPA under 3.0 as evidence of quantitative/verbal skills.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two references (academic or professional).\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Essays (written + video) — Two essays (one video and one written).\n- Resume: required — Résumé required.\n- Transcripts: required — Official transcripts from all institutions attended to earn an undergraduate degree (English translation if applicable). WES evaluations not accepted (FAQ).\n- Interview: by_invitation — Interview by invitation only.\n- Fee: $150 — waivers: Available for attending select recruitment events. Fees paid prior to waiver approval are non-refundable. — $150 application fee.\n- Other: 3-year bachelor's (except UK) generally needs additional master's/PGD for U.S. 4-year equivalence — see FAQs.\n- Other: Recommended: quantitative coursework (calculus, statistics, economics), accounting exposure, strong analytics.\n\nInternational students must submit all materials including LORs by applicable deadline for visa processing. Round 3 Feb 1 priority for UCI housing / recommended for internationals; Round 4 Apr 1 international student deadline.\n\n- [MFin Admissions](https://merage.uci.edu/programs/masters/master-finance/admissions.html)\n- [MFin FAQs](https://merage.uci.edu/programs/masters/master-finance/faqs.html)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-100.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-100. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Admissions / deadlines](https://merage.uci.edu/programs/masters/master-finance/admissions.html)\n- [Program overview](https://merage.uci.edu/programs/masters/master-finance/index.html)\n- [FAQs](https://merage.uci.edu/programs/masters/master-finance/faqs.html)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://www.reg.uci.edu/fees/2026-2027/finance.pdf)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [Merage MFin Financial Aid](https://merage.uci.edu/programs/masters/master-finance/financial-aid.html)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
