    "title": "UC San Diego Rady — MSF",
    "body": "# UC San Diego Rady — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#24 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of California, San Diego\n\nDegree route: Master of Quantitative Finance (MQF)\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUCSD Rady MQF (ex-MFin): STEM, 52 units, 12–15 mo. Fall 2027 rounds Oct 15’26–Jul 15’27 (intl Round 4 Jun 1). Program tuition Fall 2026 cohort $88,036 (+ ~$9.4k/yr campus fees); Fall 2027 rate TBD.\n\nOrientation: Fall · 12–15 months / 52 u · STEM · TFE #24 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$83,876 — Rady Master of Quantitative Finance (MQF; formerly Master of Finance) Fall 2025 cohort tuition — 52 units × $1,613/unit. PROXY for Fall 2027 — Fall 2026/2027 cohort rates not published as of asOf.; 2026–27 proxy (Fall 2025 cohort schedule on TritonLink (updated Mar 2026). Fall 2027 entering cohort rates NOT published — labeled proxy only.).\n\nCatalog id ucsd-msf maps to Rady finance master's now branded Master of Quantitative Finance (MQF); prior Master of Finance (MFin) name superseded. Self-supported; STEM-oriented quant curriculum; 52 units; billed quarterly. Deposit $1,500. QuantNet-adjacent but kept on TFE MSF slate per brief. Exclude deeper MFE/MSCF-style programs — this is the TFE #24 Rady entry. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nMandatory fees reference: $8,483. TritonLink 2025–26 Rady MQF campus/registration fees for Fall+Winter+Spring (excl. per-unit tuition) ≈ $8,483.44 including Student Services Fee, campus fees, SHIP $5,820, Rady Activity Fee, Document Fee $100. Program is 12 or 15 months — Summer quarter fees additional and not fully itemized in the F/W/S annual table. Intl Student Visa Fee $150 one-time separate. Catalog id ucsd-msf maps to Rady finance master's now branded Master of Quantitative Finance (MQF); prior Master of Finance (MFin) name superseded. Self-supported; STEM-oriented quant curriculum; 52 units; billed quarterly. Deposit $1,500. QuantNet-adjacent but kept on TFE MSF slate per brief. Exclude deeper MFE/MSCF-style programs — this is the TFE #24 Rady entry. Brief dossier records a separate Fall 2026 cohort proxy of $88,036 (52 × $1,693/unit). Catalog tuition uses the aid Fall 2025 cohort proxy $83,876 (52 × $1,613/unit). Fall 2027 entering-cohort rate is unpublished.\n\nApplication timing: Round 1 · 2026-10-15. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: required — GRE or GMAT required; application incomplete until scores verified. GRE code 4836. Waiver consideration if: bachelor’s from accredited U.S. university physically in U.S.; quantitative major; college Calculus with A/B (not Pass); cumulative GPA ≥3.00/4.00 (below 3.00 exceptional only). Request to MQF@rady.ucsd.edu with transcripts+resume.\n- GMAT: required — GMAT or GRE required. GMAT code 3NS-ZK-27. Single-sitting GMAT considered; Superscore may be supplemental. Same U.S.-degree waiver criteria as GRE.\n- TOEFL: required — min 85 — University-wide TOEFL iBT minimum 85 (new scale 4.5); Rady competitive scores above 100. Institution code 4836. MyBest not accepted. DET min 120; PTE Academic min 65 also accepted.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS Academic Band 7 minimum. Official results from test center to Rady/UCSD.\n- English waiver: Exempt if bachelor’s/master’s/doctoral with grades B (3.0)+ from regionally accredited U.S. institution with English sole instruction, or foreign institution listed in WHED as English sole language of instruction. No other documentation substitutes for WHED.\n- GPA: recommended — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — No hard MQF GPA floor stated for admission; GRE/GMAT waiver requires ≥3.00 cumulative undergrad GPA. Calculus (B+) required background; Linear Algebra (B+) highly recommended.\n- Letters of recommendation: optional — Recommendations not required; applicants without one not disadvantaged. Optional if recommender adds meaningful context.\n- Statement of purpose: optional — also known as Statement of Purpose — Statement of Purpose optional; ≤500 words, double-spaced, 12-pt. Why good MQF candidate and how Rady features benefit career; other academic/personal info welcome.\n- Resume: required — Up-to-date resume/CV; highlight quantitative/technical prep, coursework, MOOCs, research, programming, portfolios (e.g. GitHub), internships.\n- Transcripts: required — Unofficial PDF transcripts (front/back) in application; official after offer. International: certified English translation; admitted internationals must submit WES or TEC course-by-course evaluation after provisional admission.\n- Interview: by_invitation — Interviews required for admission and by invitation only; online asynchronous platform; live interview reserved in some cases. Reviewed 4–8 weeks after complete application.\n- Fee: $150 — $150 non-refundable for all applicants; credit card online or check (app held until check received).\n- Other: Strong quant foundation required; high GRE/GMAT quant expected.\n- Other: Programming/stats experience favorably considered (Python, SAS, STATA, MatLab, R, etc.).\n- Other: Fall 2027 rounds posted on admissions page (R1 Oct 15, 2026 through R5 Jul 15, 2027 domestic).\n\nDo not rely on optional SoP/LOR alone if quant evidence is thin—submit strong GRE/GMAT unless clearly waiver-eligible. Round 4 is fellowship & international deadline.\n\n- [MQF admissions](https://rady.ucsd.edu/programs/master-quantitative-finance/admissions/)\n- [MQF program hub](https://rady.ucsd.edu/programs/master-quantitative-finance/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-114.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-114. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [MQF program hub](https://rady.ucsd.edu/programs/master-quantitative-finance/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://students.ucsd.edu/finances/fees/registration/previous/2025-26/rady.html)\n- [Admissions / deadlines](https://rady.ucsd.edu/programs/master-quantitative-finance/admissions/)\n- [Tuition & aid (points to TritonLink)](https://rady.ucsd.edu/programs/master-quantitative-finance/tuition-aid.html)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://students.ucsd.edu/finances/fees/registration/2026-27/rady.html)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [Rady Fellowships](https://rady.ucsd.edu/programs/fellowships/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
