    "body": "# Utah Eccles — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#7 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: University of Utah\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUtah Eccles MSF: $39,000 flat (30 cr @ $1,300). Fall 2027: priority Feb 1 / intl Apr 1 / scholarship Jun 1 / final Aug 1.\n\nOrientation: Fall · 30 credits · $39k · TFE #7 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$39,000 — Full 30-credit program tuition at $1,300/credit (resident = nonresident); 2026–27 · as published (fixed program rate; not labeled to a single AY on page).\n\nSame rate for residents and non-residents. Fall 2027 and Spring 2027 starts. No graduate assistantships or fellowships from the program (per page).\n\nProgram page: fixed rate includes all standard fees. Living separate. Same rate for residents and non-residents. Fall 2027 and Spring 2027 starts. No graduate assistantships or fellowships from the program (per page). Program page: $39,000 for 30 credits; living separate.\n\nApplication timing: Fall 2027 Priority · 2027-02-01. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: not_required — Official admissions requirements and FAQ list do not include GRE/GMAT; not listed among required materials.\n- GMAT: not_required — Not listed among required admissions materials on MSF admissions or FAQ pages.\n- TOEFL: required — min 90 — Intl: TOEFL iBT min 90 (pre-Jan 21 2026) or 5 (on/after Jan 21 2026). Program mins higher than general Admissions Office.\n- IELTS: required — min 7 — IELTS Academic (in-person) minimum 7.0.\n- English waiver: Exemptions per University of Utah Admissions Office site. Duolingo English Test min 120 also accepted. Official score required before final decision.\n- GPA: required — minimum 3 — scale 4.0 — Bachelor’s with cumulative undergraduate GPA ≥3.0 from accredited college/university (or equivalent). Optional essay recommended if below.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 2 — Two letters required (not family/friends). Prefer professional if FT experience; faculty/advisors/internship OK. Fast Track (GPA ≥3.5 + prereqs B+) and Express Admit can forgo LORs.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Written essays / video essay — Two short essays 300–750 words: (1) overcoming adversity; (2) why MSF and career goals. Optional essay for weaknesses. Plus required video essay ≤2 minutes. Express Admit: no written essays/LORs if apply by Oct 31, 2026.\n- Resume: required — Chronological career history with dates, duties; education and certifications; international travel for school/work/residence (not vacations).\n- Transcripts: required — Unofficial from all HE institutions at apply (must show name, courses, grades, GPAs). Official after admission. Intl: NACES course-by-course eval (university covers cost after English score received).\n- Interview: unknown — Live interview not listed as required on admissions page; required video essay. Scholarship page notes interviews may factor scholarship decisions.\n- Fee: $65 — waivers: Not stated on MSF admissions page. — $55 domestic / $65 international; non-refundable.\n- Other: Prerequisites (B or better) before admit decision: Intro Accounting + Financial Management (or Series 7 / CFA L1 for finance prereq); Sophia Learning alternatives\n- Other: Fall 2027: Priority Feb 1 2027; Intl Apr 1 2027; Scholarship Jun 1; Final Aug 1\n- Other: Fast Track and Express Admit pathways\n\nIntl: Apr 1 2027 intl deadline for Fall 2027 F-1; allow time for transcript eval + official English. Complete prereqs early. Hybrid/evening options exist.\n\n- [MSF Admissions](https://eccles.utah.edu/programs/master-of-science-in-finance/admissions/)\n- [MSF FAQ](https://eccles.utah.edu/programs/master-of-science-in-finance/faq/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-091, SCH-092. MBA-only merit cards (e.g. SCH-025, SCH-052, SCH-056) are not attached to this MSF route.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-091, SCH-092. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Admissions / deadlines](https://eccles.utah.edu/programs/master-of-science-in-finance/admissions/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://eccles.utah.edu/programs/master-of-science-in-finance/tuition-scholarships-financial-aid/)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
