    "title": "UT Dallas Jindal — MSF",
    "body": "# UT Dallas Jindal — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#16 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: The University of Texas at Dallas\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nUTD Jindal MS Finance: STEM, 36 credits. Flex deadlines May 1 fall / Oct 1 spring / Mar 1 summer. Cohort ~12 mo: OOS $50k / in-state $35k; foreign deadline Apr 30. Flex COA via UTD tuition plans.\n\nOrientation: Fall/Spring/Summer Flex or summer Cohort · 36 cr · STEM · TFE #16 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$50,000 — MS Finance Cohort out-of-state / non-Texas total tuition and fees for the degree; 2026–27 · as published on MS Finance Cohort page (Fall 2027 cycle; subject to change).\n\nCFA-aligned cohort; ~12-month, 36 semester credit hours. Summer start of sequence (Semester 1 summer courses). High-achieving admits auto-considered for scholarship levels applied to tuition; awards do NOT create in-state tuition status. Cohort students excluded from general JSOM graduate scholarship portal — contact program director. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nPublished $50,000 (OOS) / $35,000 (TX resident) are total tuition and fees for the degree (includes program activities, internship/capstone, communication training, career coaching, business school per-credit fee). Living and health insurance extra. Paid in two installments (fall and spring). CFA-aligned cohort; ~12-month, 36 semester credit hours. Summer start of sequence (Semester 1 summer courses). High-achieving admits auto-considered for scholarship levels applied to tuition; awards do NOT create in-state tuition status. Cohort students excluded from general JSOM graduate scholarship portal — contact program director. SUMMER START — matriculation is not a standard autumn-only Fall intake.\n\nApplication timing: Flex — Fall regular · 2027-05-01. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GMAT/GRE not required; optional submission. Score used only if provided. GRE school code R6897.\n- GMAT: optional — Optional; use listed GMAT program codes when submitting.\n- TOEFL: required — min 80 — International applicants: TOEFL minimum 80 iBT; score ≤2 years from application date. Institutional code 6897 (FAQ).\n- IELTS: required — min 6.5 — IELTS minimum 6.5. Also accepts PTE minimum 67.\n- English waiver: Waived if bachelor's or master's earned through instruction/examination in English, or native country's primary language is English (UTD list). U.S. degree holders waived.\n- GPA: recommended — scale 4.0 — No hard minimum published. Cumulative GPA used in holistic review; currently average admitted GPA is 3.3 (FAQ / MS admissions).\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 1 — MS Finance FAQ and MS Finance Cohort page: one letter of recommendation (professional; no specific format). Note: general Jindal MS Programs Admission page states three LORs (or one if ≥2 years post-baccalaureate experience) — program-specific MS Finance materials say one.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Personal objectives statement — Personal objectives statement — one-page typed essay outlining academic interests and goals (cohort page: one-page typed; general MS page: one-page double-spaced).\n- Resume: required — Detailed résumé of work history; work experience not required for MS degrees.\n- Transcripts: required — Official transcripts from all colleges/universities; international degree certificate if applicable. Unofficial OK for decision; official before enrollment.\n- Interview: unknown — Interview not mentioned on MS Finance FAQ or Cohort application section.\n- Fee: $75 — waivers: UT Dallas students/alumni automatic waiver; military and listed Graduate Application Fee Waiver Program (U.S. citizens/PRs) per Graduate Admissions deadlines-and-fees page. — $75 non-refundable via application/Applicant Portal (UTD Graduate Admissions).\n- Other: Calculus knowledge required for MS Finance; OPRE 6303 available if missing.\n- Other: Fall deadline May 1 (FAQ); Cohort page notes Apr 30 foreign / May 31 domestic for cohort track — confirm track.\n- Other: Also accepts PTE (min 67).\n\nInternational: submit English scores and credentials early; May 1 fall deadline (or cohort foreign Apr 30). STEM program; ISSO handles I-20.\n\n- [MS Finance FAQ](https://jindal.utdallas.edu/ms-finance-faq/)\n- [MS Finance Cohort application](https://fin.utdallas.edu/ms-finance-cohort/)\n- [Jindal MS Programs Admission](https://jindal.utdallas.edu/admission-requirements/masters/)\n- [UTD Graduate Admissions deadlines and fees](https://graduate-admissions.utdallas.edu/apply-to-ut-dallas/deadlines-and-fees/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-104. MBA-only merit (SCH-057) is not attached to this MSF route.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-104. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [2026 Graduate Catalog — Finance](https://catalog.utdallas.edu/2026/graduate/programs/jsom/finance)\n- [MS Finance FAQ](https://jindal.utdallas.edu/ms-finance-faq/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://fin.utdallas.edu/ms-finance-cohort/)\n- [MS degree options](https://fin.utdallas.edu/masters-degree-options/)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [JSOM Graduate Scholarships (cohort exclusion note)](https://jindal.utdallas.edu/student-resources/scholarships/graduate-scholarships/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
