    "title": "Vanderbilt Owen — MSF",
    "body": "# Vanderbilt Owen — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#9 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Vanderbilt University\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nVanderbilt Owen MSF: STEM, 9 months, August start with Mod 0. Fall 2027 apps open Aug 19 2026; rounds Sep 10 / Oct 29 / Jan 13 / Feb 24 / Apr 28; intl visa final Apr 5 2027. Tuition 2026–27 $76,700.\n\nOrientation: Fall (Aug) · 9 months · STEM · TFE #9 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$76,700 — Owen MS Finance tuition (2026–27 AY; 9-month program); 2026–27.\n\n9-month full-time MSF. Tuition subject to change annually. Financial Aid COA also lists Owen MBA/MSF/MAcc/MMark First Year direct costs total $79,626 (tuition $76,700 + fees). All applicants auto-considered for partial merit scholarships; no need-based scholarships. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nMandatory fees reference: $2,926. Mandatory direct fees from Owen MSF tuition page / Student Accounts: Transcript $100 + Maintenance (MSF) $1,250 + Student Health Fee $882 + Student Services Fee $694 = $2,926. Health insurance $4,244 (waivable with comparable coverage) separate. Loan fees on COA page are financing estimates, not billed fees. 9-month full-time MSF. Tuition subject to change annually. Financial Aid COA also lists Owen MBA/MSF/MAcc/MMark First Year direct costs total $79,626 (tuition $76,700 + fees). All applicants auto-considered for partial merit scholarships; no need-based scholarships. Living cost band from official COA: $27,057–$32,270 (Owen MSF page Average Living Expenses sum Housing $16,030 + Food $7,488 + Personal $2,013 + Transportation $1,526 = $27,057. VU Financial Aid graduate COA First Year Indirect Total $32,270 (includes books $500 + housing $16,128 + food $7,714 + personal & health insurance $6,186 + transportation $1,526 + loan fees $216).).\n\nApplication timing: Round 1 · 2026-09-10 · 11:59 p.m. Central. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — Test-optional specialized master’s; may submit GRE if it adds value.\n- GMAT: optional — Test-optional; may submit GMAT if it adds value.\n- TOEFL: required — Official English exam or approved waiver required. Accepts TOEFL, IELTS, Duolingo, TOEFL Essentials. Code 1871 for TOEFL/IELTS. No numeric floor stated on application-instructions page.\n- IELTS: required — IELTS accepted; school code 1871. No numeric minimum stated on application-instructions page.\n- English waiver: Waiver if: undergrad degree in country where English is official language (India counted); OR lived/worked past 2+ years in such country; OR ≥90th percentile verbal on GMAT/GRE. Mark qualifications on International Applicants page.\n- GPA: not_stated — No minimum GPA stated on application-instructions page. Four-year U.S. bachelor’s or equivalent required.\n- Letters of recommendation: required — count 1 — One letter required by deadline. Prefer online form. Managers, professors, or professional colleagues OK; native-language letter + professional translation acceptable.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Personal statement / essays / video essay — Required personal statement on purpose for MSF and alignment of background/skills/interests. Optional second statement for gaps/concerns. Plus required video essay (unscripted small-talk prompts).\n- Resume: required — Current professional resume (employer-ready format) with education, work/internships, activities, interests.\n- Transcripts: required — Unofficial from every college/university at apply (name, institution, courses, grades, GPA, scale, degree date). Official prior to enrollment. Translations if not English. 3-year degrees: strongly recommend IEE/TEC course-by-course equivalency.\n- Interview: by_invitation — Essential; by invitation on rolling basis after complete application. Asynchronous Kira: 4 oral + 1 written response. Denial/waitlist possible without interview; offer of admission requires evaluative interview.\n- Fee: $100 — waivers: Not detailed on application-instructions page (check FAQ/admissions for exceptions). — $100 application fee for MS Finance.\n- Other: Apr 5, 2027 final deadline for international applicants (visa processing)\n- Other: Complete apps due 11:59pm Central on round deadline\n- Other: Preliminary Financial Declaration for intl (no bank statements at apply)\n\nIntl: Apr 5 2027 hard final; English waiver or official scores early (10–14 days to post). 3-year degree holders: get credential eval ready. Interview invitation needed for admit.\n\n- [Application instructions](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/masters-in-finance/admissions/application-instructions/)\n- [Admissions overview](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/masters-in-finance/admissions/)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-096. MBA-only merit (SCH-051) is not attached to this MSF route.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-096. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Admissions / deadlines](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/masters-in-finance/admissions/)\n- [Application instructions](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/masters-in-finance/admissions/application-instructions/)\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/masters-in-finance/admissions/tuition-financial-aid/)\n- [Curriculum / STEM](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/masters-in-finance/curriculum/)\n- [Apps open Fall 2027](https://business.vanderbilt.edu/news/2026/08/14/vanderbilt-business-applications-fall-2027-open-august-19/)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n- [VU Costs – Graduate 2026–27](https://www.vanderbilt.edu/financialaid/costs-graduate/)\n- [Student Accounts Grad/Prof Tuition 2026–27](https://www.vanderbilt.edu/stuaccts/fees/tuition_fees_2026-27_grad_prof/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
