    "body": "# WashU Olin — MSF\n\nChecked: 19 October 2026. Preliminary program research.\n\n## Ranking and degree route\n\n#3 in TFE Times Best Master's of Finance (as of 2026-10-26).\n\nBatch 1–4 (2026-10-26): TFE Times 2026 ranks 1–30 ingested. Locked unranked adds on this slate: florida-msft, chicago-booth-mif, columbia-msfe. US News Finance MBA specialty is not used as an MSF program rank. Quant/MFE is a separate quant-mfe track ranked by QuantNet 2026; those eight rows keep tfeRank2026 null and are not merged into TFE ranks 1–30.\n\nRanking provenance: [TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/).\n\nUniversity: Washington University in St. Louis\n\nDegree route: MS in Finance\n\nApplication status: Route identified · 2027 eligibility to verify\n\n## Academic direction\n\nWashU Olin MSF: three concentrations. Fall 2026-start tuition $81,500 (Corporate, 2 sem) or $102,900 (Quant / WAM, 3 sem) + per-semester fees.\n\nOrientation: 2–3 semesters · 3 concentrations · TFE #3 (2026)\n\nFaculty and supervision: Individual faculty specialties and master’s supervision access have not yet been verified.\n\n## Tuition and application timing\n\n$81,500 — Corporate Finance concentration total tuition (Fall 2026 starters, 2 semesters); 2026–27 (Fall 2026 starters; Fall 2027 cohort rates not yet separately posted as of asOf).\n\nFlat program tuition; three concentrations with different length/cost. Page labels costs for candidates starting Fall 2026. Living/health insurance not in tuition. Fall 2027 intake context.\n\nAlternate format: Quantitative OR Wealth & Asset Management total tuition (Fall 2026 starters, 3 semesters) $102,900. Per semester posted Spring 2026: program fee $900 + student government $100 + health/wellness $350 = $1,350/semester. Corporate (2 sem) ≈ $2,700 fees; Quant/W&AM (3 sem) ≈ $4,050 fees. Health insurance separate (required). Flat program tuition; three concentrations with different length/cost. Page labels costs for candidates starting Fall 2026. Living/health insurance not in tuition. Flat program tuition for Fall 2026 start candidates; living/health insurance separate.\n\nApplication timing: Concentration-specific deadlines not fully captured this pass — site/brief to fill on next scrape of apply pages.. Confirm deadline time zone and personal requirements on the official page.\n\n## Application requirements\n\nAs of 2026-10-27.\n\n- GRE: optional — GMAT or GRE not required but recommended for most candidates. GRE code 6929. Online GMAT/GRE accepted.\n- GMAT: optional — Not required but recommended. MS Finance GMAT code R4T-WG-53. Official scores released when submitting application.\n- TOEFL: required — min 90 — Intl applicants must submit official English scores valid through application deadline. TOEFL iBT/Home: 5.0 overall (new scale) OR ≥90 old scale (page also lists 4.5). ETS code 6929.\n- IELTS: required — min 6.5 — IELTS Academic minimum 6.5. Send electronically selecting Washington University in St. Louis Graduate Programs.\n- English waiver: Exemption possible per university exemption criteria; request in application portal; Office of the Provost reviews. Also accept GATEWAY English (495) and Duolingo (125).\n- GPA: not_stated — No numeric minimum GPA on on-campus SMP apply page; committee considers strong undergraduate GPA among factors if omitting test.\n- Letters of recommendation: not_stated — Official on-campus specialized master’s checklist does not list letters of recommendation.\n- Statement of purpose: required — also known as Personal statement / career essay — Personal statement (500-word max) on life experiences shaping decision to apply and how Olin helps long-term goals. Plus required career essay (100-word max) on ideal post-graduation career. Optional essay 250 words.\n- Resume: required — One-page resume required.\n- Transcripts: required — Unofficial transcripts accepted for decision; official required before orientation if enrolling. Bachelor’s equivalent at enrollment; most intl 3-year degrees OK. Non-English: original + English translation. WES/ECE not required.\n- Interview: not_stated — On-campus SMP apply page does not list an interview (online SMP lists application video interview).\n- Fee: $0 — waivers: N/A — no fee charged. — No application fee for on-campus specialized master’s programs.\n- Other: Prerequisites vary by concentration: Quant Finance & Wealth/Asset Management need Statistics + Calculus I; Corporate Finance reviewed holistically\n- Other: Fall 2027 rounds: Oct 8 2026, Jan 7, Feb 25, Apr 15 2027 then rolling\n\nIntl: English scores by deadline; apply earlier rounds for visa time. No app fee. Confirm concentration prerequisites (esp. Quant). Optional GMAT/GRE still recommended for many.\n\n- [On-campus SMP apply](https://olin.washu.edu/programs/specialized-masters/on-campus-smp-apply.php)\n\n## Internships\n\nProgram-specific internship structure, placement rates and international-student outcomes have not been verified. Ranking or location alone does not establish how easy an internship is to obtain.\n\n## Funding\n\nProgram-tied funding verified 2026-10-26: SCH-087. MBA-only merit cards (e.g. SCH-025, SCH-052, SCH-056) are not attached to this MSF route.\n\nShared scholarship IDs: SCH-087. See the [scholarship library](../../04-scholarships/README.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Official tuition / budget](https://olin.washu.edu/programs/specialized-masters/ms-in-finance/cost-aid-scholarships.php)\n- [Corporate curriculum](https://olin.washu.edu/programs/specialized-masters/ms-in-corporate-finance/curriculum.php)\n- [TFE Times 2026 MSF rank via TFE Times](https://tfetimes.com/best-finance-program-rankings/)\n\n## Outstanding evidence\n\n- Fall 2027 tuition, mandatory fees and total degree budget\n- Individual faculty fit and availability for master’s supervision\n- Internship outcomes with cohort, denominator and international-student breakdown\n- Personal scholarship eligibility and deadlines\n- THE / QS comparison in the correct category\n"
