    "path": "04-scholarships/opportunities/iit-stuart-graduate-merit.md",
    "title": "Illinois Tech Stuart Graduate Merit Scholarships (MS Finance) (SCH-116)",
    "body": "# Illinois Tech Stuart Graduate Merit Scholarships (MS Finance) (SCH-116)\n\n- **Category:** Merit-Based · **Type:** scholarship\n- **Status (2026-10-26):** Automatic with admission\n- **Scope:** iit-msf\n- **Programs:** iit-msf\n- **HK eligible:** yes · **TW eligible:** yes · **International:** yes · **PRC:** yes\n\n## Summary\nAll Stuart School of Business graduate students are automatically reviewed for merit-based scholarship awards at the time of admission. Award availability and amounts vary by program; amounts are tiered based on academic credentials. Awards prorated evenly across courses needed for the degree; deferrable up to one year. International students may also be awarded need-based aid during admission. University graduate scholarships page: ~30–40% of graduate students receive scholarships annually. Citizenship not restricted on Stuart merit language.\n\n## Eligibility\nAdmitted Stuart graduate students including MS Finance. Beacon Education / Coursera enrollees not eligible.\n\n## Amount\nVaries / tiered; amounts not published on Stuart page\n\n## Deadline\nWith admission (no separate application)\n\n## Notes\nOpen external MSF (AMP Plus One is optional undergrad path, not required).\n\n## Sources\n- [Stuart Scholarships and Aid](https://www.iit.edu/stuart/admission-aid/scholarships-and-aid)\n- [Finance M.S. — Scholarships and Aid](https://www.iit.edu/academics/programs/finance-ms)\n- [Graduate Student Scholarships](https://www.iit.edu/admissions-aid/tuition-and-aid/scholarships/graduate-student-scholarships)\n\n_Do not treat amounts/deadlines as final; re-verify on the official page before applying._\n"
