    "body": "# Qualcomm Innovation Fellowship (North America) (SCH-045)\n\n- **Category:** Company-Sponsored · **Type:** fellowship\n- **Status (2026-10-26):** 2027 North America cycle published · abstract window closed (Oct 19, 2026) · amount verified\n- **Scope:** 25 listed US/Canada universities\n- **Programs:** cmu-mscs, mit-cs, princeton-cs, stanford-cs, berkeley-cs, ucla-cs, ucsd-cs, ucsb-cs, illinois-cs, maryland-cs, columbia-cs, usc-cs, cornell-cs, michigan-cs, washington-cs, gatech-cs, texas-cs, wisconsin-cs, purdue-cs\n- **HK eligible:** unclear · **TW eligible:** unclear · **International:** unclear\n\n## Summary\nTeam-based (2 PhD students) research fellowship.\n\n## Eligibility\nPhD students at listed universities (incl. MIT, Stanford, UCLA, UC Berkeley, Cornell, Georgia Tech per 2026 rules); nationality: unclear.\n\n## Amount\n'Cash awards of $50,000 per Entrant will be awarded to the university academic departments of the winning students, not to the winning Entrants directly' (2027 Official Rules PDF, verbatim)\n\n## Deadline\n2027 cycle abstract/application due Monday Oct 19, 2026 by 10:00 a.m. (ASU Inner Circle program notice; Official Rules defer to Website timeline) — window closed as of 2026-10-26\n\n## Sources\n- [QIF 2027 Official Rules (PDF)](https://www.qualcomm.com/content/dam/qcomm-martech/dm-assets/documents/QIF-2027-official-rules-US-CANADA.pdf)\n- [Qualcomm press note — 2027 QIF launch (Oct 12, 2026)](https://www.qualcomm.com/news/releases/2026/10/qualcomm-launches-2027-innovation-fellowship-program-for-north-a.md)\n- [ASU Inner Circle — apply by Oct 19, 2026](https://innercircle.engineering.asu.edu/2026/09/apply-for-the-2027-qualcomm-innovation-fellowship-by-oct-19/)\n\n_Re-verify on the official page before applying._\n"
