    "title": "Santa Clara Leavey MSFA Merit-Based Scholarships (SCH-120)",
    "body": "# Santa Clara Leavey MSFA Merit-Based Scholarships (SCH-120)\n\n- **Category:** Merit-Based · **Type:** scholarship\n- **Status (2026-10-26):** Automatic with admission (priority Apr 1)\n- **Scope:** santaclara-msf\n- **Programs:** santaclara-msf\n- **HK eligible:** yes · **TW eligible:** yes · **International:** yes · **PRC:** yes\n\n## Summary\nMerit scholarships automatically considered at application. For on-campus MSBA/MSFA/MSIS beginning Fall 2026 awards page: awarded to applicants with GMAT/GRE at or above average (650 GMAT / 315 GRE); priority to April 1 Priority Deadline submitters. Scholarship range $2,000–$8,000. Majority of merit awards go to students who officially submit GRE/GMAT and apply by priority deadlines; test-waiver students risk reduced eligibility. Citizenship not restricted on MS scholarship section.\n\n## Eligibility\nAdmitted on-campus MSFA students. Priority deadline April 1. Online MSFA awards not covered by this on-campus table.\n\n## Amount\n$2,000–$8,000\n\n## Deadline\nWith admission; priority April 1 for Fall\n\n## Notes\nPage labels awards for students beginning Fall 2026 — confirm Fall 2027 cycle ranges when updated.\n\n## Sources\n- [Leavey Graduate Business Scholarships — MS](https://www.scu.edu/business/scholarships/)\n- [MSFA Cost & Financing](https://www.scu.edu/business/ms/ms-finance-and-analytics/)\n\n_Do not treat amounts/deadlines as final; re-verify on the official page before applying._\n"
