    "title": "Villanova School of Business MSF Merit Scholarships (SCH-101)",
    "body": "# Villanova School of Business MSF Merit Scholarships (SCH-101)\n\n- **Category:** Merit-Based · **Type:** scholarship\n- **Status (2026-10-26):** Post-admit Scholarship Request Form\n- **Scope:** villanova-msf\n- **Programs:** villanova-msf\n- **HK eligible:** yes · **TW eligible:** yes · **International:** yes · **PRC:** yes\n\n## Summary\nVSB offers merit scholarships to academically and professionally accomplished students. After admission, applicants submit a Scholarship Request Form via the Application Status Page. Holistic review of rigor of coursework, undergraduate GPA, standardized test scores, and professional background. Funding limited and first-come/first-served within the cycle — apply early. Typically one-time awards. Cannot be combined with MSF Fellowship (SCH-102).\n\n## Eligibility\nAdmitted Villanova MSF students who submit the Scholarship Request Form. International students are eligible for merit scholarships after admission (not eligible for federal aid).\n\n## Amount\nNot published (varies; notified after request review)\n\n## Deadline\nAfter admission via portal; funding limited — early rounds preferred (intl recommended Round 2 Jan 15)\n\n## Notes\nFellowships cannot be combined with VSB merit scholarships.\n\n## Sources\n- [Villanova MSF Admissions / Scholarships](https://www.villanova.edu/university/business/academics/graduate-programs/msf/admissions.html)\n- [Villanova MSF International — merit eligibility](https://www.villanova.edu/university/business/academics/graduate-programs/msf/international-students.html)\n\n_Do not treat amounts/deadlines as final; re-verify on the official page before applying._\n"
